1 _UID 34861569AE5C46A5857A64025887E72D850A
1 _AMTID 162143272695:1030:164657654
1 CHAN
2 DATE 2 NOV 2019
1 NOTE  ALIAS: Raoul I Comte de Bayeux
2 CONT
2 CONT The following information was contained in a post-em from Curt Hofeman n
2 CONC :
2 CONT
2 CONT Count d'Ivry [Ref: Tompsett, Wm Conqueror]
2 CONT half-brother: Richard I Duke of Normandy [Ref: ES III:694A]
2 CONT
2 CONT ...Richard the Fearless' mother, Espriota, married, in the troublous t i
2 CONC mes of his boyhood, a rich countryman called Sperling. They had a so n c
2 CONC alled Raoul of Ivry, who seems to have been high in power and favo r wi
2 CONC th the second Richard, his half-brother... [Ref: The Normans by Sa rah O
2 CONC rne Jewett, Chapter V, DUKE RICHARD THE GOOD http://www.public.co e.edu
2 CONC /~theller/soj/nor/nor05.html]
2 CONT
2 CONT Douglas mentions a 'half' brother of Richard, who assumed the title o f c
2 CONC ount between 1006 and 1011.  p.89  A clearer example of the acquisi tio
2 CONC n by a feudal family of lands which had earlier been part of the du cal d
2 CONC emesne, can be seen in the descent of the possessions of Count Ru dolf, h
2 CONC alf-brother to Duke Richard I.  Among the lands held by this ma n were e
2 CONC states situated on the Risle near Saint Philibert; estates o n the Eure
2 CONC , including Concherel, Jouy, and, it would seem, Pacy; land s dependent o
2 CONC n Breteuil; and lands centered on Ivry.  Many of these la nds, particul
2 CONC arly those on the Eure, were inextricably intermingled wi th the earlie
2 CONC st demesne of the Norman duke and must have come to Rudul f through his s
2 CONC tepfather or his half-brother.  Their subsequent devolu tion is thus of p
2 CONC articular interest.  Part of Ivry lands went to the c ount's eldest son H
2 CONC ugh, bishop of Bayeux, while the barony of Saint Ph ilibert passed thro
2 CONC ugh the count's second son, John bishop of Avranche s, to that cathedra
2 CONC l church.  But the larger part of Rudolf's possessi ons, including the h
2 CONC onour of Pacy and the district honour of Breteuil , descended through t
2 CONC he count's daughter, Emma, to her husband Osbern , the steward of Duke R
2 CONC obert I, and one of the guardians of the infan t William. [Ref note: th
2 CONC e previous URL of the online source of this i s no longer valid & a goo
2 CONC gle.com search did not show a new URL ... Cur t 01/01/03]
2 CONT
2 CONT The ducal family of Normandy early determined to have an historiograph e
2 CONC r whom they sought in France, one Dudon, dean of the chapter of St. Q u
2 CONC entin, who between 1015-30 wrote in Latin half verse, half prose, a h i
2 CONC story of the family according to the traditions and accounts transmit t
2 CONC ed to him by Raoul, Count of Ivry grandson of Rollo and brother of Ri c
2 CONC hard I Alinea. [Ref: Catholic Encyclopedia http://www.newadvent.org/c a
2 CONC then/11104a.htm]
2 CONT
2 CONT Happy New Year!
2 CONT Regards,
2 CONT Curt
2 CONT
2 CONT ************
