1 NAME Gunnora) "not" de Crepon Gunnor /(Gundra/
2 GIVN Gunnora) "not" de Crepon Gunnor
2 SURN (Gundra
1 SEX F
1 _UID 469A32A4D9A94AD0B2742B1D54C627494AA1
1 _AMTID 162143272696:1030:164657654
1 CHAN
2 DATE 2 NOV 2019
1 NOTE  MARRIAGE:  A Danish wife Curt Hofemann, curt_hofemann@yahoo.com, i n a p
2 CONC ost-em, wrote:
2 CONT
2 CONT Apparently she was not "de Crepon" & her parentage is unknown:
2 CONT
2 CONT The name of the father of Gunnor is unknown. Herbastus is derived fro m t
2 CONC he name of her brother Herfast/Arfastus, but is unsupported. [Ref : Tod
2 CONC d A Farmerie <taf2@po.cwru.edu> message to Gen-Medieval 6 Nov 199 6]
2 CONT
2 CONT The greater part of our information about Gunnor and her relations i s d
2 CONC erived from those additions to the History of William of Jumieges f or w
2 CONC hich Robert de Rotigny is responsible. It is Robert who preserve d the s
2 CONC tory of how Richard I of Normandy became enamored of the beauti ful Sen
2 CONC frie, wife of one of his foresters, and how Senfrie contrived t o subst
2 CONC itute her sister Gunnor for herself, to the Duke's ultimate sat isfacti
2 CONC on. [Ref The Sisters and Nieces of Gunnor, Duchess of Normand y by G.H. W
2 CONC hite in the Genealogist, New Series 1921 v37 p57]
2 CONT
2 CONT Parentage of Gunnor and her siblings is unknown. While some sources ca l
2 CONC l her father Herfastus, this was in fact the name of her brother. Sh e h
2 CONC as also been claimed as a daughter of the Danish royal family, bu t the
2 CONC re is no evidence for this, and the context of her coming to atte ntion o
2 CONC f Richard I and the family's subsequent rise to power militate s agains
2 CONC t her being a royal daughter. Douglas argued, based on the don ations o
2 CONC f brother Arfast to the monastery of St. Pere, that the root o f the fa
2 CONC mily was in the Cotetin region of Normandy, but van Houts ha s suggeste
2 CONC d that the Cotetin land was granted to Arfast, rather than i nherited b
2 CONC y him. Thus we are left with the more ambiguous statement o f Torigny a
2 CONC nd others that she was a member of a Norman family of Danis h origins. [
2 CONC Ref: Todd A Farmerie <taf2@po.cwru.edu> message to Gen-Med ieval 5 Jan 1
2 CONC 997]
2 CONT
2 CONT Gunnora ... was not "de Crepon", nor was she daughter of Herbastus d e C
2 CONC repon of Denmark - her brother Herfastus/Arfast appears to have rec eiv
2 CONC ed Crepon only after Gunnora took up with Richard I, and thus the f ami
2 CONC ly was not originally from there.  Likewise, while she is said to b e o
2 CONC f a noble family of Danish ancestry, it is not stated that her fath er w
2 CONC as from Denmark (the family probably arrived with Rollo, in the ge nera
2 CONC tion of her (unknown) grandfather. [Ref: Todd A Farmerie <taf2@po. cwru
2 CONC .edu> message to Gen-Medieval 28 Jul 2000]
2 CONT
2 CONT Research note 1: Was her father Herfast de CREPON or King Haraldblaafa n
2 CONC d of DENMARK&#00063; There is a lack of consensus on this. -Charlotte '
2 CONC s Web Genealogy http://www.charweb.org/gen/rjones/d0042/g0000020.htm# I
2 CONC 239
2 CONT
2 CONT Research note 2: father: Harald I Blaatand, Bluetooth, King of Denmar k [
2 CONC Ref: McBride2 (possibly citing Wurts)]
2 CONT
2 CONT My notes on Gunnora:
2 CONT This is the same Gunnora known as Gunnora of Crepon, but both are of l i
2 CONC ttle value.  Gunnora was NOT of Denmark.  Some inventive genealogis t s
2 CONC omewhere along the line decided to make her daughter of Harald Blue too
2 CONC th, but there is no basis for this, and what we know of her indicat es i
2 CONC t is not really a possibility worthy of consideration.  Her nephe w lat
2 CONC er was called "of Crepon" but he likely gained his possessions th rough G
2 CONC unnora's marriage to the Duke, rather than this representing th e origi
2 CONC nal home of the clan.
2 CONT
2 CONT What can be said of Gunnora's parents&#00063;  Nothing!  She was not d a
2 CONC ughter of Harfast, as (too) often stated.  Her family was likely of t h
2 CONC e minor Norman nobility, since her oldest sister was married to a for e
2 CONC ster at the time Richard first bumped into the girls.  That's it.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard I of Normandy first bedded, and later married Gunnora, whose a n
2 CONC cestry is entirely unknown.  She is sometimes said to be daughter o f a K
2 CONC ing of Denmark, but this is incorrect. [taf]
2 CONT
2 CONT There are several things going on here.  First of all, the father of G u
2 CONC nnora and siblings is not known.  Attempts to name him Herbastus prob a
2 CONC bly originated in confusion with her brother.  Second, Gunnora had th r
2 CONC ee sisters, Senfria/Senfreda, Wevia, and (Avelina).  The first marrie d a
2 CONC n otherwise unknown forester.  The latter two are confused by our t wo s
2 CONC ources, one claiming that it was Wevia who married Osbern, and th e oth
2 CONC er that Wevia married Turold of Pont Audemer, and by deduction, ( Aveli
2 CONC na) married Osbern.  We know that Osbern married one of them, an d a re
2 CONC cent analysis suggests that it was Wevia for nomenclatural reaso ns. (S
2 CONC pecifically, Turold and wife had a granddaughter named Duvelina , and i
2 CONC t is hypothesized that she was named for her grandmother, and t hat Duv
2 CONC elina is the authentic name of the sister, rather than Avelina . Finall
2 CONC y, in which generation was Osbern's.  This is unambiguous.  Sh e was si
2 CONC ster of Gunnora and the others.  There is no source before rec ent time
2 CONC s that claims otherwise.  There are two probable origins for t he error t
2 CONC hat she was niece of Gunnora.  First, due to the error in na ming her f
2 CONC ather Herfastus, someone aware that this was the name of Gun nora's bro
2 CONC ther assumed then that Avelina's father was Gunnora's brothe r (the nam
2 CONC e of Gunnora's father being unknown, and probably unknowable ).  The se
2 CONC cond possibility is a confusion of uncle and nephew.  Harfas tus/Arfast h
2 CONC ad a son Osbern of Crepon, and perhaps someone confused th is man with O
2 CONC sbern of Bolbec.  Still, we know for certain that Osber n of Bolbec mar
2 CONC ried a sister of Gunnora. [Ref: Dave Utzinger <UTZ@aol. com> message to G
2 CONC en-Medieval 29 Jul 2000]
2 CONT
2 CONT Regards,
2 CONT Curt
2 CONT
2 CONT *******
