1 NOTE  MISC:  CHARLEMAGNE and his brother CAROLMAN, were crowned King of Fran k
2 CONC s 18 Oct 768, each ruled half of the kingdom.  In his long life CHARL E
2 CONC MAGNE had 9 wives and many children, however only two of his childre n h
2 CONC ave descendants that lasted for more than 2 generations.  The end o f h
2 CONC is conquest was the beginning of Hold Roman Empire.  In 800 the Emp ero
2 CONC r Charlemagne was crowned by the Pope as ruler of a massive Empie w hic
2 CONC h encompassed modern France, Italy and most of Germany.  In 843, i t wa
2 CONC s divided between his grandsons, West Francia, or France, being gi ven t
2 CONC o Charles the Bald.  During the next century the authority of th e Caro
2 CONC lingian rules in France gradually collapsed, and in 987 they wer e repl
2 CONC aced by Hugh Capet and his line.
2 CONT
2 CONT OCCUPATION:  King of Franks 747-814, crowned Holy Roman Emperor 25 De c 8
2 CONC 00; one of the great men in history.  CHARLEMAGNE is credited wit h bui
2 CONC lding churches, founding schools and restoring monasteries.  Howe ver, h
2 CONC e had created an empire too rapidly for it to be ruled with hi s limite
2 CONC d means.  His countries were overseen by special envoys who tr avelled i
2 CONC n pairs, one layman and one clergyman, and reported their tri ps to him
2 CONC , confirming the oaths of fealty.
2 CONT
2 CONT His immense achievement was fragile, as was demonstrated by his succes s
2 CONC ors.  However, his prestige remained intact.  He is buried at Aix-la- C
2 CONC hapelle in a circular church, and both CHARLES V and BONAPARTE, on th e e
2 CONC ve of their becoming emperors, came to kneel before his tomb.
