1 NOTE  CONFLICT: Chapman Family History, Beauchamp William Chapman, private p u
2 CONC blishing County, 1987 (states: HAROLD III GORMSON, Blaastand (Bluetoo t
2 CONC h) or HAROLD VII)
2 CONT
2 CONT OCCUPATION:  First Chrsitain king of Denmark, was born 911, in the tim e o
2 CONC f Rollo the Dane.  Harold died 986.
2 CONT
2 CONT BIRTH:  Twin
2 CONT
2 CONT MISC:  Harald refused to accept the crown until he had first performe d h
2 CONC is father's obsequies with all the magnificence becoming his high r ank
2 CONC . One of his earliest was the conquest of Norway, which became a pr ovi
2 CONC nce of Denmark. Styrbear, King of Sweden, solicited the aid of Kin g Ha
2 CONC rold in one of his wars, and to enforce his request he brought alo ng w
2 CONC ith him Gyntha, his sister, a lady of admirable beauty. The strata gem h
2 CONC ad the intended effect; Harold Bluetooth became enamored and marr ied h
2 CONC er. Theprogress of Christianity gained some headway during his re ign, a
2 CONC nd the King received baptism, and erected a splendid church. Hi s daugh
2 CONC ter Gunilda married Richard I, Duke of Normandy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:  Harrison's History of Yorkshire; Preface and Charts.
2 CONT Britannica Encyclopedia, Vol. 26, p. 224; Vol. 12, p. 179; Vol .                 2
2 CONC 0,p. 4; Vol. 28, p. 767.
2 CONT Williams' Historians History of the World, Vol. 16, pp. 37-49.
2 CONT Edward S. Lewis Manuscripts, pp. 164, 162, 226, 274.
2 CONT The Plantagenet Ancestry, by Lt. Col. W. H. Turton, pp. 26-7.
