2 CONC arried Pricess Judith, widow of Ethelwolf, King of England and dau . of C
2 CONC harles the Bald, King of France and grandson of Charlemagne.  I t is be
2 CONC lieved that Baldwin's father may have been Anarcher, Great Fore ster, o
2 CONC f Flanders who died in A.D. 837.  Baldwin I was known as "Bra s de Fer,
2 CONC " or "Iron Arm."  Judith's father, Charles the Bale establish ed Baldwi
2 CONC n as the first Count of Flanders. At the time and for 300 yea rs prior, t
2 CONC he Northmen were ravaging the coast of Flanders and attacki ng the sett
2 CONC lements along the river.  In light of these circustances, i t seems pla
2 CONC usible that the King saw in Baldwin a strong and powerful l eader who c
2 CONC ould control this area and, therefore, a son-in-law of poli tical exped
2 CONC iency.
