1 NOTE  The name of Bidford is a corruption of its original appellation, By-th e
2 CONC -ford.  The manor was settled by William the Conqueror on his consor t M
2 CONC atilda, and was given by William Rufus to Sir Richard de Grenville , wh
2 CONC ose descendants resided her and at Kilkhampton, in Cornwall, for m any g
2 CONC enerations; and three of them represented Devon in Parliament. [B rad V
2 CONC erity, citing White's Devonshire Directory of 1850]]
2 CONT ----------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Louise Staley, in her post to SGM, citing "A History of the Granvill e F
2 CONC amily, etc.", has Richard as brother of Robert Fitz Hamon and son o f H
2 CONC amon (Dentatus), while I have Richard as brother of Robert Fitz Ham on a
2 CONC nd son of Hamon (Dapifer).  The brother is the same, but maybe he r sou
2 CONC rce missed a generation (Dapifer).
2 CONT
2 CONT *********The name of Bidford is a corruption of its original appellati o
2 CONC n, By-the-ford.  The manor was settled by William the Conqueror on hi s c
2 CONC onsort Matilda, and was given by William Rufus to Sir Richard de Gr env
2 CONC ille, whose descendants resided her and at Kilkhampton, in Cornwall , f
2 CONC or many generations; and three of them represented Devon in Parliam ent
2 CONC . [Brad Verity, citing White's Devonshire Directory of 1850]]
2 CONT ----------------
2 CONT Louise Staley, in her post to SGM, citing "A History of the Granvill e F
2 CONC amily, etc.", has Richard as brother of Robert Fitz Hamon and son o f H
2 CONC amon (Dentatus), while I have Richard as brother of Robert Fitz Ham on a
2 CONC nd son
2 CONT of Hamon (Dapifer).  The brother is the same, but maybe her source mis s
2 CONC ed a generation (Dapifer).
2 CONT
2 CONT ***********
