2 CONT An account of Hamo, who was son of Hamo Dentatus (slain at Val-es-Dune s i
2 CONC n 1047), and who was dapifer both to the Conqueror and William Rufu s a
2 CONC nd sheriff of Kent in 1086, is given, together with an account of h is s
2 CONC ons Hamo and Robert, by D. C. Douglas in "The Domesday Monachoru m of C
2 CONC hrist Church Canterbury", pp. 55-6, where the relevant authoriti es are c
2 CONC ited. That Hamo dapifer and Hamo the Sheriff were undoubtedl y one and t
2 CONC he same person is proved by the Kentish returns of 1242-3 i n 'The Book o
2 CONC f Fees', pp. 654 et seq., when the lands held by the sher iff in 1086 w
2 CONC ere held by the earl of Gloucester, who was the heir of H amo dapifer t
2 CONC hrough the marriage of Robert earl of Gloucester with th e daughter and h
2 CONC eir of Robert, son of Hamo dapifer.  [Origins of Som e Anglo-Norman Fam
2 CONC ilies]
2 CONT
2 CONT *******Alternate name found in file: Hamo De Crevequer
2 CONT
2 CONT Fought at the Battle of Hastings in 1066.
