2 CONC , was the son of Sybil, daughter of Sir Robert Corbet, of Alcester , Co
2 CONC unty Warwick, and having m. &#00063;Mabel, daughter and (in her is sue) h
2 CONC eir of William Fitz Richard, a man of huge estates in Cornwall , was cr
2 CONC eated about Apr 1141, Earl of Cornwall, probably by the Empres s Maud, b
2 CONC ut the title was fully recognised subsequently by King Stephe n.  He wa
2 CONC s a witness to the compromise between Stephen and Henry, 1153 .  Sherif
2 CONC f of Devon, 1173-75.  He was in command, ex parte Regis, Oc t 1173, aga
2 CONC inst the rebellious Barons.  He d. spm legit, at Chertsey , Surrey, 1 J
2 CONC uly 1175, and was buried in the Abbey of Reading, when th e Earldom rev
2 CONC erted to the Crown.  [Complete Peerage, III:429 as correc ted by XIV:20
2 CONC 7]
2 CONT
