1 NOTE  JOHN DE MOHUN, son and heir by 1st wife. He was a knight. He married J o
2 CONC an, 5th daughter of William (DE FERRERS), EARL OF DERBY, younger sist e
2 CONC r of his stepmother and coheir of their mother. He was living 29 Jul y 1
2 CONC 253, but died v.p., 1253-54, in Gascony. His heart was buried at Ne wen
2 CONC ham Abbey, and his body at Bruton. His widow's marriage was grante d to P
2 CONC iers de Chauvent, but bought of him for 200 marks by Sir Rober t AGUILL
2 CONC ON, whom she married in or before August 1256. She died befor e June 12
2 CONC 69, and appears to have been dead in October 1267.  [Complet e Peerage I
2 CONC X:21, (transcribed by Dave Utzinger)]
