2 CONC eath date.  I believe that it is in error, maybe referring to Willi am I
2 CONC 's death in 942.  Also note that Theobald I, Count of Blois, was i nvol
2 CONC ved in William I's treachorous ambush and murder in 942 and marrie d Lu
2 CONC itgarde, his widow, the next year 943.
2 CONT ---------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Curt Hofemann, curt_hofemann@yahoo.com, write in a post-em:
2 CONT
2 CONT The dates are further conflicted by other sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT birth:
2 CONT (915/20) [Ref: ES II:79] parenthesis = approximation
2 CONT 915/20 [Ref: ES III:49]
2 CONT abt 920 [Ref: Moriarty p6, 228]
2 CONT abt 930 [Ref: Moriarty p36]
2 CONT
2 CONT married to Guillaume, Duc de Normandie/William "Longsword" Duke of Nor m
2 CONC andy, Count of Rouen:
2 CONT um 940 [Ref: ES II:79] (um = about/around)
2 CONT
2 CONT married to Theobald I 'Le Tricheur' Count of Blois, Seigneur de Montag u
2 CONC :
2 CONT date: 942/45 [Ref: ES III:49, Moriarty p228]
2 CONT 943/44 [Ref: ES II:46]
2 CONT 943/5 [Ref: Moriarty p36]
2 CONT abt 945 [Ref: Moriarty p6]
2 CONT
2 CONT died:
2 CONT 27.V nach 977 [Ref: ES II:79] (nach = after)
2 CONT 27.V nach 978 [Ref: ES III:49]
2 CONT 9.II nach 978 [Ref: ES II:46]
2 CONT Feb 9 978 [Ref: Moriarty p228, p36]
2 CONT after Feb 9 978 [Ref: Moriarty p6, Paget p135]
2 CONT
2 CONT Regards,
2 CONT Curt
2 CONT
2 CONT **********
