1 NOTE  OCCUPATION:  King of Germany 939-973, Emperor 962-973; Crowned 962.  S p
2 CONC ent early years of reign in subduing revolts of nobles; aided ADELAID E
2 CONC , Queen of Lombardy, against BERENGAR II (951); married ADELAIDE; def e
2 CONC ated Hungarians in great battle of the Lechfield (955); defeated BERE N
2 CONC GER II (961).  Coronation (962) revived the empire of CHARLEMAGNE.  D e
2 CONC posed Pope John XII. His son OTTO
2 CONT crowned as joint emperor (967) by Pope John XIII.  ADELAIDE was dau. o f K
2 CONC ing RUDOLPH II of Burgundy who m. LOTHAIR, son of King HUGH of Ital y.  S
2 CONC he was imprisoned by BERENGER II, appealed to OTTO I who came t o her r
2 CONC escue and married her, his second wife.  As queen mother durin g reign o
2 CONC f her son OTTO II (973-983), she had much influence in admini stering t
2 CONC he state affairs.  Joint regent with Empress THEOPHANO for OT TO III.  S
2 CONC he died in cloister in Selz, Alsace, 16 Dec. 999.
