2 CONT Sir Walter de Lindissi or Lind(e)say (almost certainly 3rd son of Gilb e
2 CONC rt de Ghent) probably accompanied David, Earl of Huntingdon, subseque n
2 CONC tly King David I, in his anglicising of the Lowlands in the early 12t h c
2 CONC entury; he was witness 1116 to an inquisition concerning the see o f Gl
2 CONC asgow.  [Burke's Peerage]MISC:  Also spelled GAUT
2 CONT
