2 CONT "Chico Enterprise Record, Thursday, April 5, 1973.  Hattie J. Noe.  Fu n
2 CONC eral services will be held at 11 A.M. Saturday in the Hall Van Hook F u
2 CONC neral Chapel for Hattie J. Noe, 96.  Mrs. Noe, of Cactus Avenue, die d W
2 CONC ednesday in a local convalescent hospital after an extended illness .  B
2 CONC orn Sept. 12, 1876, in College City, she was raised at the famil y home o
2 CONC n Rock Creek.  She attended schools in Chico and a country sch ool in B
2 CONC ella Vista, Shasta County.  She married Clinton J. Noe in Nove mber 190
2 CONC 2 in Oroville.  Their daughter, Virginia, died in early childh ood.  Th
2 CONC e Noes established a grape stake business in Mendocino Count y and rais
2 CONC ed cattle, turkeys and chickens after returning to the Chic o area.  No
2 CONC e died in 1925.  Mrs. Noe continued to live on the ranch be fore moving t
2 CONC o her home on Cactus Avenue in 1951.  She was a member o f the Church o
2 CONC f Christ of Chico.  Mrs. Noe is survived by numerous cou sins.  Dr. Cha
2 CONC rles Adams of the Church of Christ will officiate at th e services.  Wa
2 CONC va Backlund will provide chapel music and the Laburnu m Avenue Young Pe
2 CONC oples Chorus will sing "In the Sweet Bye and Bye" an d "Hide Thou Me."  P
2 CONC rivate interment will follow at the Chico Cemetery . ..."
