1 NOTE  The following is an account by Eva Mann Tull of her marriage and time s w
2 CONC ith George Edward Tull, compiled by Fern Repetti and presented at t he M
2 CONC ann family reunion in June 1976:  "The Tull Family.  George Edwar d and E
2 CONC va Alice Mann married 27 Oct 1901, in Chico, California, by th e Justic
2 CONC e of the Peace.  Eleven children were born.-----We were marrie d 27 Oct 1
2 CONC 901, went to Thermalito and stayed with Jim and Katie Elli s for ten da
2 CONC ys.  We then went to Rackerby, Yuba County, at Ed's home [ her brother-
2 CONC in-law] until March 17.  We came back to my father's mil l and Martin w
2 CONC as born Sept. 1, 1902, at Cohasset.  Then we took up a h omestead on Bu
2 CONC ckeye and moved there after the mill shut down about 2 0 Oct. 1902.  We s
2 CONC tayed for three months or maybe only six or eight we eks - then went do
2 CONC wn to the old Guss Darge ranch to cook and wash fo r him, while Hattie w
2 CONC ent away to get married.  We stayed there until t he last of January an
2 CONC d then rented my mother's old place and Jim was b orn there 1 Dec. 1903
2 CONC .  Then we left the old home place in July 1904 a nd went to Inwood, Sh
2 CONC asta County, to haul lumber.  We rented an old ra nch and Jesse was bor
2 CONC n Feb. 7, 1905 - from there we moved to Ted Bridg es or Norton Ranch or S
2 CONC ilvers place - stayed all winter and moved in M arch to Dunnegans Hall w
2 CONC here Vernon was born 19 Oct 1906.  Then when V ernon was ten days old, w
2 CONC e moved into the Marsh house and Lemm was bor n there 1 Oct. 1908.  The
2 CONC n we bargained for a home on 160 acres of Gra ndad Tull's ranch.  We ha
2 CONC d several head of cows, some hogs, and a fou r horse team.  We built a f
2 CONC our room cabin.  We moved there in March, a nd Elmer was born 26 May 19
2 CONC 10.  Bill was also born in this house 10 Ja n 1912, and we were sold ou
2 CONC t in March of 1914 and had to move, so we w ent to Anderson in the Goff h
2 CONC ouse and Claude was born there 15 June 19 14.  Then we moved out of tow
2 CONC n north to the Ficas place - we stayed he re two years and in early Nov
2 CONC ember of 1917, we moved back toward tow n two miles in the Miller house a
2 CONC nd Fern was born 28 Nov. 1917.  Fro m here in the spring of 1918, we we
2 CONC nt to Siskiyou County.  We went t o Dorris and seventeen miles beyond t
2 CONC o a mill (Topsy).  Everyone got s ick.  Jessie died 20 Apr 1918, and ev
2 CONC erything was bad.  We lived in Do rris that winter --had the flu -- wen
2 CONC t back to mill at Welters nine mi les from Dorris for the summer -- the
2 CONC n back to Chico in about middle o f September of 1919, to work in the r
2 CONC ice, and in  November, bought th e place on Linden Street.  Bula was bo
2 CONC rn 2 Dec 1919 at 15th and Laure l Streets ten days before moving into t
2 CONC he house on Linden Street.  W e lived in this house all the time going t
2 CONC o the mountains for the summ ers.  Iris was born here 9 June 1925.  We a
2 CONC lso went to Dorris the summ er when Bula was six months old.  It was ou
2 CONC t last trip to Dorris (ne w mill above Welters).  Then in August of 193
2 CONC 5, we went to Ukiah -- ca me back to Chico 22 Mar 1940."
