1 NOTE  Chico Enterprise-Record, Chico, Calif. Saturday, 12 Feb. 1983, p. 2A :  "
2 CONC Obituraries.  GEORGE GRIFFITH.  George Ellis Griffith died Thursda y at h
2 CONC is Chico home.  Griffith was born Mar. 26, 1900, to Mary Mann Gr iffith a
2 CONC nd George Griffith of Chico, where he was reared and went to s chool.  H
2 CONC e graduated in 1923 from the Chico Normal School and taught s chool for o
2 CONC ne year in Gridley and two years in Hamonton.  He then remo ved to Thor
2 CONC nton where he served as School Administrator of the New Hop e School un
2 CONC til his retirement in 1953.---Following his retirement, h e returned to C
2 CONC hico where he was an orchardist.  Griffith was a 50-yea r member and pa
2 CONC st master of the Galt Masonic Lodge #267.  Survivors in clude his son J
2 CONC ohn of Chico; a daughter Evelyn Free of Redding; a brot her, Homer, of S
2 CONC acramento; a sister, Ardye Poff of Paradise; eight gra nd children and t
2 CONC wo great-grandchildren.  Services will be held at 1 0 A.M. Monday at Br
2 CONC usie Funeral Home.  Burial will be in Fall River Mi lls Cemetery."
