1 NOTE  CHICO ENTERPRISE RECORD, no date:  "Gerry Mann.  Dayton----A gravesid e s
2 CONC ervice for Gerald Spencer Mann, 88, of Dayton, will be held at 10 a .m. S
2 CONC aturday, July 24 at the Chico Cemetery.  He died Tuesday, July 20 , 199
2 CONC 9, at a local hospital.  Mann was born July 11, 1911, to Maude an d Har
2 CONC ley Mann, Butte County pioneers, in Chico.  On April 15, 1935, h e marr
2 CONC ied Vergie Perdue.  At a young age, Mann began working for the B utte C
2 CONC ounty Road Department.  He later built roads in Chester.  Durin g World W
2 CONC ar II, he worked at the Chico Air Base.  Mann farmed for Fani ani and F
2 CONC ish in Durham, and later worked at the Llano Seco Ranch for 1 9 years.  I
2 CONC n 1977, he and his wife retired to Dayton.  Mann loved hunt ing and fis
2 CONC hing and was a member of the Durham Odd fellows.----Survivo rs include h
2 CONC is wife, Vergie of Dayton; two sons, Joy [&#00063;} of Chi co, and Alle
2 CONC n of Hillsboro, OR; a brother, William of Kingman, AZ; fou r grandchild
2 CONC ren and five great-grandchildren...."
