2 CONT Obituary:  REDDING, Shasta, CA:  "Claude Tull.  Graveside services fo r C
2 CONC laude M. Tull, 90, of Redding will be at 10 a.m. Thursday at Anders on'
2 CONC s District Cemetery.  Mr. Tull died Wednesday, July 7, 2004, at hi s re
2 CONC sidence.  Born June 15, 1914, in Anderson, he moved back to Shast a Cou
2 CONC nty in 1996 from Auburn.  He was an electrician for McClellan Ai r Forc
2 CONC e in Sacramento, a former member of the Masonic Lodge in Folso m and th
2 CONC e Forester Lodge in Sacramento.  Survivors include son Gary o f Clackam
2 CONC as, OR; daughters Claudia Arlint of Springfield, OR; Doroth y Hardy of H
2 CONC ouston; and Betty LaLonde of Carson City, NV; brother Elme r of Sacrame
2 CONC nto; sister Iris Owens of Sparks, NV; and six grandchildre n.  Memorial c
2 CONC ontributions can be made to the Mercy Hospice, 1544 Mark et St., Reddin
2 CONC g, CA 96001.  Arrangements are being handled by Anderson 's Chapel in A
2 CONC nderson."
