1 NOTE  "When Doug Mann's father, Arthur Riley Mann, was 12 years old, he wa s e
2 CONC ngaged by Ben Crouch, a wealthy valley landowner and builder of Wes two
2 CONC od, to bring 12 mules over the summit from Big Meadows (now Lake Al man
2 CONC or) to the Crouch ranch near Chico.  Riding alone on a saddle hors e an
2 CONC d driving the mules took Arthur five days, with an overnight sto p at t
2 CONC he Jonesville Hotel both coming and going.  In relating this exp erienc
2 CONC e, Arthur, who was a carpenter by trade and often made repairs t o the h
2 CONC otel for Mrs. Minderman, never once indicated that the hotel h e had st
2 CONC ayed in as a boy differed structurally from the present hote l (Mann 19
2 CONC 94, interview)."  Source:  A SMALL CORNER OF THE WEST, Butt e Meadows, C
2 CONC hico Meadows, Jonesville, CA, p. 118.
2 CONT
2 CONT Butte County Delayed Birth Records, CA:  Arthur Riley Mann, born Nov . 2
2 CONC 4, 1890, at Cohasset, Butte County; father Joseph Aaron Mann, bor n Iow
2 CONC a; mother Melvina Ann Yancey, born Utah.  Supporting evidence:  A ff. M
2 CONC rs. Nora W. Cook, sister, Nov. 13, 1951; Aff. Laura E. Duensing , siste
2 CONC r, De. 10, 1951; Appl. United Benefit Life Ins. County, Pol # C -474 38
2 CONC 5, Nov. 17, 1943.  Filed June 5, 1952, No. 98-269, pg. 108.
