2 CONT "Arthur Mann, was born in the same state, and died at the age of sixty -
2 CONC six.  The Mann family is of English origin, the progenitor of the fam i
2 CONC ly in the United States having crossed the Atlantic and made settleme n
2 CONC t in Virginia about 1630; the family were represented in Jamestown wh e
2 CONC n it was burned by the Indians in 1632."  Source:  History of Butte C o
2 CONC unty 1918 by Mansfield, p. 1212.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Arthur Mann, thought to have been born at sea, 3 Feb. 1768, m (1) Nan c
2 CONC y Banks Thompson m(2) --------1815.  Eight children, but some uncerta i
2 CONC nty as to whether all were by first wife, as reported (1874).  (In th e a
2 CONC ccount of Eva (Mann) Tull, Chico CA (1976), son Arthur A. Mann, b . 181
2 CONC 8.)  Children of Arthur Mann Sr.:
