1 NOTE  !SOURCE: records and oral history in posession of Douglas W. Garner.
2 CONT
2 CONT Annie Laurie Linn Ford (Linn) saw her first car in Welch, WVA; moved d u
2 CONC ring the first grade to Charleston.  Papa came back from France in 19 1
2 CONC 8 (about the 9th grade), and became principal at Dunbar HS in 1919 .  S
2 CONC he attended Dunbar HS for 4 years.  "Met Phil at 15 years old, i n Dunb
2 CONC ar."  After HS, Phil went to Chicago to technical school, and t o Marsh
2 CONC all College, WVa University.  His brother George went to Idiana .
2 CONT
2 CONT Linn taught in Nitro while Phil finished college.  He worked at Dupon t i
2 CONC n Baltimore, MD, before moving to Cleveland, Ohio.  The Saunders ha d c
2 CONC ome from Montgomery, and lived on the riverbank of the Kanawah Rive r.  P
2 CONC hil's older brothers had gone to France during war.  Phil was th e only o
2 CONC ne of the brothers to go beyond the 8th grade.  The lived in R ondan, 2 m
2 CONC i. south of Montgomery.
2 CONT
2 CONT They married in Dunbar, at the Baptist Church, a plain frame building ; a
2 CONC nd resided in the Oakland subdivision of Baltimore.
