2 CONT T.F. Hebb, of English descent, son of Thomas Hebb, was born 1823; marr i
2 CONC ed 1842 to Catherine, daughter of Hiram Sanders; his wife died in 185 3
2 CONC , and he married Mary Ann, daughter of Levi Lipscomb. Children Sara h A
2 CONC ., Thomas F., John C., Joseph H., and Martha E.; lives 5 miles belo w S
2 CONC t. George on a farm of 175 acres, of which 75 acres are improved; h as b
2 CONC een in Tucker since 1876; has held several offices in the county ; he w
2 CONC as on the board of supervisors in 1866, and held office until th e cons
2 CONC titution went out of force; held the position of president of th e boar
2 CONC d of education for 12 years. in 1861, he entered the Union army , and r
2 CONC emained in it until 1865; was a Rowlesburg when Jones made hi s raid in
2 CONC to that quarter; was in several skirmishes and in one of the m had his k
2 CONC nee thrown out of place, from the effect of which his righ t side has e
2 CONC ver since been helpless.
2 CONT Buried Macedonia Cemetery
2 CONT [Brøderbund WFT Vol. 11, Ed. 1, Tree #1647, Date of Import: Nov 8, 199 8
2 CONC ]
