1 NOTE  !REL: Saunders Family Tree; Imperfect Genealogy of the Saunders Family
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH: Letter; ledger entries, etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT Letter from Texas, from Mary Roper to "Uncle Saunders" stating that he r f
2 CONC ather was Benjamin Elisius Rober, son of _____ Roper who died Feb 2 8, 1
2 CONC 827 who died and discussing whether or not the statute of limitati ons h
2 CONC ad expired.  The letter is not dated but included a bill from Wal l & S
2 CONC tabe, Morticians dated Oct. 2 1889 & Nov 1 1899(marked duplicate ) and i
2 CONC ndicating that she had already made a partial payment toward th e full c
2 CONC ost.  The bill and the letter tie in with notes and a letter f rom H.M.
2 CONC Tyler, Richmond attorney for heirs of Rev. David Roper who dis owned hi
2 CONC s children when they "went to business."  This also ties in wi th ledge
2 CONC r entries and reciepts (Virginia.) on funeral expenses for How ard Chin
2 CONC n Saunders.  Mary jRopers letter concludes with mention of "Un cle Bran
2 CONC ch" and Rosa Jones.  jTaylor's Virginia. Baptist Ministers giv es a goo
2 CONC d account of Rev. David Roper (1792-1827).  The question, howe ver, rem
2 CONC ains as to what Howard Chinn S. was doing in the Houston are a and what M
2 CONC ary Roper's connection to the Saunders family actually was .  Her lette
2 CONC r is that of an obviously educated, mature woman.  (JWS re search notes
2 CONC )
