1 NOTE  Sir Walter Hungerford, KG(1421), 1st Lord (Baron) Hungerford, so creat e
2 CONC d by writ 7 Jan 1425/6; born c22 June 1378; knighted 1399, MP: Wilt s 1
2 CONC 400, 1404, 1407, 1413 and 1414 and Somerset 1409, Speaker of Hous e of C
2 CONC ommons 1414, Sheriff of Wilts 1406 and Somerset and Dorset 1414 ; envoy t
2 CONC o the Holy Roman Emperor Sigismund 1414 and subsequently Sigi smund's M
2 CONC aster of the Household when the latter visited England 1416 ; served in H
2 CONC undred Years War, allegedly won a duel against Charles V I of France be
2 CONC fore Calais 1401, fought at Agincourt 1415 (the spoils a rising from wh
2 CONC ich he allegedly used to restore Farleigh Castle, thoug h he may also h
2 CONC ave raised the money from ransoming the eight distingui shed Frenchmen h
2 CONC e took prisoner after the Agincourt Campaign), command ed naval force w
2 CONC hich in 1416 relieved Harfleur (captured by Henry V th e previous year i
2 CONC n the campaign that culminated in Agincourt) from a F rench blockade, e
2 CONC nvoy to negotiate with Archbishop of Cologne 1417 an d present at succe
2 CONC ssful Siege of Rouen by Henry V 1418; Steward of th e Household to Henr
2 CONC y's V and VI, Constable of Windsor Castle 1417, Mem ber of Council of R
2 CONC egency 1422, Lord High Treasurer 1426-1432; marrie d 1st by 18 Sep 1402 K
2 CONC atherine (died on or after 14 June 1426), younge r daughter and coheir o
2 CONC f Thomas Peverell, of Cornwall; married 2nd b y 8 May 1439 Eleanor (die
2 CONC d 1 Aug 1455), daughter of Sir John Berkeley , of Beverstone, Glos, and w
2 CONC idow of (a) 13th/6th Earl of Arundel and ( b) Sir Richard Poynings, and d
2 CONC ied without having had further issue 9 A ug 1449.  [Burke's Peerage]
