1 NOTE  !REL: Saunders Family Tree (PAS, Sr.), JWS research notes; lived eas t s
2 CONC ide of Cleveland Ohio along Euclid and Rt. 20 per PASjr.
2 CONT
2 CONT !HISTORY:
2 CONT (Mary Welby Baker) m. 1907: prob. Putnam County/Mason County, W.Virgin i
2 CONC a.  Orvil Leonard Baker, probably gr. son of Charles (1815) and Salli e (
2 CONC b.1820) Baker of Kason County, W.Virginia. He was born near Leon, W .Vi
2 CONC rginia. and his brothers and sisters were: George, Raymond, Charles , a
2 CONC nd sister, Clero.  Raymond went to Gallipolis, Ohio, Charles went t o C
2 CONC harleston, W Virginia.  The mother of these children made her hom e wit
2 CONC h or near Raymond in Ohio.  She died in auto accident near Charle ston, W
2 CONC .Virginia in 1940's or 1950'2. (O.L. Baker had an "Uncle Jasper " who w
2 CONC as son of Charles & Sallie Baker of Mason County W.Virginia.)
2 CONT
2 CONT !OCCUPATION:
2 CONT Orvil, know as O.L., worked for the railroad.  He was first a telegrap h
2 CONC er, then agent.  His work took him to several areas...first in W.Virg i
2 CONC nia(Ritchie County) where his wife, Welby, met and introduced the Sau n
2 CONC ders brothers to the Robertses family resulting in the later marriag e o
2 CONC f T.D. Saunders to Jeanne Roberts.  The Bakers later went to Ohio , fin
2 CONC ally retiring to the Cleveland area where the main part of this f amily i
2 CONC s still located.  Issue:...
