1 NOTE  PER SAUNDERS FAMILY TREE, PER JWS - m. 11 APR. 1805 By Rev. Archibal d A
2 CONC lexander [Per Private Francis Saunders - Capt. Wm. Moseley's Compan y o
2 CONC f Cavalry attached to 1st Regiment Virginia. Militia under Gen. Cha mbe
2 CONC rlyne.  Served Aug. 29-Sept 18, 1814.  Bounty was approved.]  Deat h pe
2 CONC r exerp. War of 1812 Bounty Land papers, his estate accounts - fro m pe
2 CONC rsonal and business papers, ledger books, letters of Geo. D. sen t to t
2 CONC he Virginia State Library, titled "Saunders Business Papers."
2 CONT
2 CONT The Farmville Journal - Oct. 25, 1866   On the 10th day of November ne x
2 CONC t will be offered for sale to the highest bidder, on the premises, th e t
2 CONC ract of land on which Francis Saunders, deceased resided, containin g 6
2 CONC 18 acres, more or less, lying in the county of Buckingham (Virginia ), 1
2 CONC 2 miles north of the Courthouse, and 1 mile from New Store, on th e Old S
2 CONC tage Road.  There are on this place a comfortable dwelling hous e, with 5 r
2 CONC ooms and all needful out-houses.  At the same time and plac e, will be o
2 CONC ffered for sale: one tract of land containing 145 acres, l ying on both s
2 CONC ides of Willis River but no houses on it.  Terms at sale . (Ad signed_ G
2 CONC eor. D. Saunders Ex'or. of F. Saunders, Dec'd.
2 CONT [the above is a Prince Edward County paper and directions are from the r
2 CONC e. Example...12 miles north of the courthouse means from Pr. Ed. Coun t
2 CONC y Courthouse.]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1863 War Map and Land Ownership Map - west and slightly north of New S t
2 CONC ore: Mrs. Saunders, Sallie B. & Francis's farm (the dots indicate bui l
2 CONC dings, etc.) West and slightly north is Geo. D.'s residence.  Anothe r S
2 CONC aunders is located lower on the land ownership map.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Francis Saunders, my father, inherited Tudor Hall, the old home of hi s f
2 CONC ather on Willis River and the mill which was shortly thereafter des tro
2 CONC yed by fire, about 1830.  He married 1807 Sallie Penick, the younge st d
2 CONC aughter of Wm. and Judith Penick, who had been Judith Walker of Ap pomm
2 CONC attox River, Prince Edward County, Virginia. just above "Walker' s Ford
2 CONC " now Willbournes Bridge and lived in Buckinham County near th e road f
2 CONC rom New Store to the C.H.[courthouse] until their deaths, hi s in 1845 a
2 CONC nd hers in 1864.  They left five daughters: Jedidah M., Eli xabeth Mose
2 CONC ley, Judith L., Sarah F., Martha S. and one son, George Dou glas Saunde
2 CONC rs." [from An Incomplete Genealogy of the Saunders Family , G.D.Saunder
2 CONC s]
2 CONT
2 CONT !CENSUS: data on file
2 CONT
2 CONT !SOUCE:  Saunders family tree; Saunders Imperfect Geneology; JWSaunder s r
2 CONC esearch notes.
