2 CONT 1  NAME William /Smute/
2 CONT 2  GIVN William
2 CONT 2  SURN Smute
2 CONT 2  NSFX --C--T
2 CONT
2 CONT William Smute/Smoot as a member of the Boatwrights Guield in London i n 1
2 CONC 633 agreed to perform 50 days of work (boatbuilding) in Virginia fo r C
2 CONC ol. Thomas Burbage and shortly (1634) sailed for Virginia. King Jam es I o
2 CONC f England had died in 1625 leaving the throne to his son Charle s I who d
2 CONC issolved Parliament for 11 years, increased taxes with risin g prices a
2 CONC nd left common men in distress at the time William left Engl and. At th
2 CONC e time he arrived in Virginia, the worst problems of coloniz ation were b
2 CONC ehind and a population of 3,000 was established, 5,000 i n 1645 with ra
2 CONC pid growth thereafter to 22,000 in 1700.
2 CONT
2 CONT He left Virginia for Charles County, MD in 1646 where he establishe d a s
2 CONC hipyard on the west bank of the Wicomico. There were only 400 whi tes i
2 CONC n the County in 1658 and only 2,800 by 1700. In 1790 the total po pulat
2 CONC ion was 20,600 b&w souls with a rapid
2 CONT decline thereafter especially whites. (The Price of Nationhood, 1994 ) (
2 CONC Smoot, Steve L., (smoots@compuserve.com), 1/7/97, download from aol .co
2 CONC m, File: Smoot/Bryant/Parrish)
2 CONT
2 CONT Other Sources:
2 CONT Ref.: WFT Vol. 1, #5009
2 CONT Ref.: WFT Vol. 2, #5282
2 CONT (Chinn)
