2 CONT WILL of JOHN CHYNN/CHINN SR.
2 CONT dtd. Dec. 15, 1691 - probate May 11,1692, Lancaster County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT In the name of God Amen the fifteenth day of December Ano Dni 1691 I J o
2 CONC hn Chinn Senr of the County of Laneacter (vente being in sound and Pf e
2 CONC ct memory thanks bee to Almighty God and calling to remembrance the u n
2 CONC certaine State of this transitory life and that all fflesh must yiel d u
2 CONC nto death when it shall olease to God to call Doe make constitute o rda
2 CONC in and Declare this my last will and Testament in manner and form e fol
2 CONC lowing, revooking and adnulling by these psnts all and evray Test amt a
2 CONC nd Testamts Will and Wills heretofore by me made declared eithe r by wo
2 CONC rd or writing and this to bee taken only for my last will and T estamt a
2 CONC nd none other. And first penitent and sorry from the bottom o f my hear
2 CONC t for my sins past most humbly desiring forgiveness for the s ame I giv
2 CONC e and comitt my soule unto God my Saviour and Redeemer in who me and by t
2 CONC he meritts of Jesus Christ I trust and believ assuredly t o be saved an
2 CONC d to have full remission of all my sins and that my soul e with my body a
2 CONC t the  Generall day of Resurrection shall rise again e to Joy and throu
2 CONC gh the merits of Christs death and passion possess a nd inherit the Kin
2 CONC gdom of Heaven ppared for his blest and chosen and m y body to bee buri
2 CONC ed in such place where it shall my Executrs hereafte r named to appoint A
2 CONC nd now for the setling of my temporall Estate an d such goods Chattells a
2 CONC nd debts as I am now possest with and it hat h pleased God farr whome m
2 CONC y deserts to bestow upon me I doe order an d dispose of the same in man
2 CONC ner and forme following that is to say Ite m I give unto my loving wife A
2 CONC lice Chinn my saddle horse and all my fu rniture thearunto belonging ca
2 CONC lld by the name of Dragon and alsoe he r riding horse with all the furn
2 CONC iture belonging called by the name o f Hester.
2 CONT Item I give unto my Sone John Trussell and my daughter Elizabeth Truss e
2 CONC ll his wife twelve pence apiece to bee paid to him six months after m y d
2 CONC ecease.
2 CONT Item I give unto my son Thomas Chilton and my daughter Sarah Chilton h i
2 CONC s wife twelve pence apiece to bee paide within six months after my de a
2 CONC th.
2 CONT Item I give unto my Daughter Ann Chinn all that tract of Land be it mo r
2 CONC e or less whereon Thomas Chilton now lives which I bought from Richar d L
2 CONC loyd laying upon the heade of Powells Creek and to her heirs foreve r I g
2 CONC ive unto my said Daughter Ann one ffeatherbed a pair of blanket s A Rug
2 CONC g a boulster and one pillow, one Iron Pott, a frieng pan, A Mar e with a
2 CONC ll her increase running in Kirbys neck fouor sheep twelve hea d of catt
2 CONC le when she shall come to the age of sixteen years and not be fore.
2 CONT Item I give unto my daughter Katherine Chinn All the Right and title w h
2 CONC ich I have to a tract of Land laying at the heade of Morattico whic h I p
2 CONC urchased of Thomas Maddison to her and her heirs forever, tenn he ad of c
2 CONC attle four sheep a mare A
2 CONT Rugg, bolster, and one pillow one iron pott a frieng pan when she shal l c
2 CONC ome to the age of sixteen years and not before.
2 CONT Item I give unto my sone John Chinn twelve pence in money to bee paid e h
2 CONC im within six months after my decease because I have paid and hee h ath r
2 CONC ecd his portion already.
2 CONT Item I give unto my Sone Rawleigh Chinn All the tract of Land I now li v
2 CONC e upon, and to his heirs forever, One ffeather bed and furnitur One i r
2 CONC on pott, ffour sheep, tenn head of cattle, one mare three years old w i
2 CONC th all her increase forever, two
2 CONT Guns and a paire of Andjions when hee shall come to the age of twent y y
2 CONC eares and not before and also one Negro between sixteen and twenty.
2 CONT Item My will and pleasure is that all the said cattle and sheep soe gi v
2 CONC en unto my saide children as aforesaide as they shall come to their r e
2 CONC spective age or ages to bee delivered as aforesaide the cattle shal l n
2 CONC ot exceed ten years apiece nor
2 CONT the sheep to exceed five years apiece.
2 CONT Item My will and pleasure is that all my Estate both chattle and psona l
2 CONC l Except before excepted given and bequeathed as aforesaide I give un t
2 CONC o my Loving wife Alice Chinn whome I make whole and sole Executrix o f t
2 CONC his my last will and Testament
2 CONT In witness whereof I have hereunto set my hand and seale the day and y e
2 CONC ar above written
2 CONT Signed sealed published and declared this to bee
2 CONT my last will and Testament in psence of us
2 CONT William Smith,  Alexander Dune,
2 CONT Edward Geffery John Chinn (Seal)
2 CONT
2 CONT Probate fuit, etc. Lancaster Court May 1692 sworn to by Alexr Dune Edw d G
2 CONC effery in court
2 CONT Mr. John Stretchley, Cl. Ct.
2 CONT
2 CONT Copied from a photostat obtained from The Virginia State Library by Na n
2 CONC on
2 CONT L. Carr, 6102 the Paseo, Kansas City 10, Mo.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Note by N.L.C. - the use of ff as in fflesh is for a capital F)
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of John Chinn, Alice Chinn married John Stretchley (cl e
2 CONC rk of the court), whose will dated 6 Dec. 1698 was proved 14 Dec. 169 8
2 CONC .
2 CONT Alice was Exrx. He died in 8 Dec. 1698 in his 50th year.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Compiler's Note: Copied from a typewritten copy in the Chinn Family
2 CONT file #73 developed by Miss Nanon L. Carr and located in the Mid-Contin e
2 CONC nt Genelogy Library,  Independence
2 CONT Ref.: Haydens Virginia Genealogies, p. 299. (Also see: Jones, Our Roya l A
2 CONC ncestors, pp 28)
2 CONT March 8, 1669, Elizabeth (Hussey&#00063;) Travers (wife of Rawleigh Tr a
2 CONC vers&#00063;)
2 CONT app'd her son William Travers, her Att'y to acknowledge to John Chin n t
2 CONC he
2 CONT "qr. pt." of her mill. (IV., 96) At the same time Raweligh Travers and
2 CONT Elizabeth Travers signed the contract; and p. 128, John Chinn and
2 CONT Elizabeth (Shearman or Travers&#00063;) Chinn signed the contract.
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE: Many researchers identify Elizabeth Travers as the first wife of
2 CONT John Chynn. There seems to be sufficcient evidence that she was NOT th e
2 CONT wife of this John Chynn. Although it appears that she was in fact
2 CONT married to a John Chynn, how & where she fits in is still to be resolv e
2 CONC d.
2 CONT (jcd 6/6/96)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref.: W. G. Stannard, Virgina Historical Society, Richmond, Virginia . A
2 CONC pril
2 CONT 26, 1916 Letter to Mrs. Wm. Rodes, 152 N. High Street, Lexington, KY
2 CONT John Chynn emigrated to Virginia sometime before July 1662. Settled in
2 CONT Lancaster County, Virginia, later moved to Morattico County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref.: WFT V1 #5169 John (Chynn) Chinn came from England on the "James
2 CONT
2 CONT Moratico" to Virginia in 1660 and settled in Lancaster County, Virgini a
2 CONC . He was a
2 CONT planter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: may have been son of John Chynn and Sarah Yates. This John being
2 CONT the son of Sir Thomas. (jcd 8/30/95)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref.: Wm. & Mary Quarterly Vol 17, July 1908, page 63.
2 CONT Lancaster Recorder, - On December 6, 1694 it was stated that Ann daugh t
2 CONC er
2 CONT of John Chinn would be 13 years old on May 5 next. (dob would have bee n
2 CONT May 5, 1682). Rawleigh son of same, 11 years old on May 23 next. (dob
2 CONT would have been May 23,1684) and Catherine, (m. George Heale) dau of s a
2 CONC me
2 CONT would be 9 on June 7 next. (dob would have been June 7, 1686)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref.: Virkus, Frederick Adams, The Abridged Compendium of American
2 CONT Genealogy, Vol. I, 1925, page 546.
2 CONT Ref.: Bentley, E. P., indexed, Genealogies of Virginia. Families (fro m W
2 CONC m. &
2 CONT Mary Qtrly.), Vol III, Hale - Musco, 1982, pp. 1, 4, 630
2 CONT John Chinn appears in Lancaster County, Virginia., in 1664. He owned l a
2 CONC nd on
2 CONT Morathis (&#00063;) Creek. The Chinns, Balls, Downmans, and all settle d i
2 CONC n that
2 CONT part, and intermarried. The McCartys came later.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Chinn had the following children: i. John T., m. Elizabeth. ii.
2 CONT Ann, m. (1) William Fox, (2) Richard Chichester. iii. Sarah, m. ____
2 CONT Chilton. iv. Katherine, m. _______ McCarty. v.. Rawleigh, m. Esther
2 CONT Ball. vi. Joseph. vii. William.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref.: Haydens Virginia Genealogies, p75: July 3, 1662
2 CONT Thomas Williams, of Morattico, sold to John Chynn, of Morattico, Lanc' r
2 CONT County, planter, and Henry Davys, of do., shipwright, a tract of 372 a . o
2 CONC f
2 CONT land given to David Fox by Gov. Berkley, and on which Williams then
2 CONT lived. (L. II. 239) John Chinn also received 100 a. on Morattico creek ,
2 CONT Lan'r (Lancaster) County, Aug.24, 1664, for 2 heads, also 370 a. some
2 CONT locality, March 17, 1667-8 (vi. 63, 113 Virginia. Land Bank), formerl y g
2 CONC ranted
2 CONT to David Fox, gent; also same date, John Chynn and Gilson Chynn receiv e
2 CONC d
2 CONT grant of 550 a. Rapp. County for 11 head rights. April 26 1670, 220 a.
2 CONT granted Thomas Wright and John Chynn for 5 heads. (id. vi. 276)
2 CONT
2 CONT (QUESTION&#00063; Is Glison Chynn, the brother of John, and was the fa t
2 CONC her
2 CONT Thomas&#00063;)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref.: Davis, Virginia Lee Hutchenson, "Tidewater Virginia Families",
2 CONT 1989, page 96
2 CONT April 24, 1668, John Mayo patented land on the south side of the
2 CONT Rappahannock River upon the main branch of Dragon Swamp. The land
2 CONT adjoined that of Jno. Chyn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref.: Doris Wallace, P.O. Box 35, Clarence, MO 63437
2 CONT "Family Group Sheet" for - John Chinn
2 CONT Dec 15 1691 date of will, proved May 1692
2 CONT Ms. Wallace Ref., The Chinn Book, p. 1 - 6
2 CONT Ms. Hazel Chinn Besserer&#00063;
