1 NOTE  WILL of ALICE STRETCHLEY
2 CONT dtd 29 August 1701 - probate 8 October 1701, Lancaster County, Virgini a
2 CONT Lancaster County, Wills, etc. No 8 (1690-1709) pp. 210-211
2 CONT In the Name of God Amen. I Alice Stretchley of the parish of St Mayrie s
2 CONC ,
2 CONT White Chapell in the County of Lancr being sick & weak of body & sound
2 CONT and perfect in mind & memory praise be threrfore given to Almighty God
2 CONT doe make and ordain this my present last will & testamt in manner and
2 CONT form following that is to say first and princably I comend my Sole int o
2 CONT the hands of Almighty God hoping through the Merrits death and passio n o
2 CONC f
2 CONT My Sav Jesus Christ to have full and free pardon and forgovness of al l m
2 CONC y
2 CONT sins and to inherit everlasting life and my body I committ to the eart h
2 CONT to be decently buried at the descretion of my Exr hereafter named an d a
2 CONC s
2 CONT touching the disposall of my temporall estate as it hath pleased God t o
2 CONT bestow upon me I give and dispose as followeth.
2 CONT Imprimis I will that my debts and funerall charges be paid & discharge d
2 CONC .
2 CONT Item I give unto my Daughter Ann Fox three silver Spoons the great Sil v
2 CONC r
2 CONT Tankard marked AS and one Silvr Tumbler of the middle size and all my
2 CONT wearing cloaths that came out of England this year from Mr Ellis and m y
2 CONT Plush Sadle.
2 CONT Item I give unto my Daughter Cathrine Heal all my Stock of Cattle hogg s
2 CONT and sheep that is upon my plantation that my husbabd Mr. Jno Stretchle y
2 CONT bought of Mr William Tomlyn Except four Cowes and Six Sheep which I gi v
2 CONC e
2 CONT to my Sister Dorothy Durham.
2 CONT Item I give unto my Daughter Cathrine Heal one of the smallest silver
2 CONT Tankards & one of the smallest Silvr Tumblors and three Silvr Spoons a n
2 CONC d
2 CONT one hundred fourty and five pounds Sterling being due to me and in the
2 CONT hands of Mr Tho Ellis Merchant of London and one negro woman named Su e o
2 CONC f
2 CONT Short Stature and one negro man named Jack and one black mare Runeny a t
2 CONT Morratico Point branded on the rear Buttook and shoulder with JC.
2 CONT Item I give to the sd Cathrine Heal two featherbeds with ruggs &
2 CONT blanketts and four pare of sheets three pillows and six pillow cears s i
2 CONC x
2 CONT pewter dishes tow pewter Basons one Doz of plases one doz. wooden ditt o
2 CONT and one pewter Chamber pott six Leather Chairs out of the new house
2 CONT Chamber and one suit of my best wearing cloaths Excepting them before
2 CONT given to my Daughter Anne Fox this being in Lieu and full satisfactio n o
2 CONC f
2 CONT her portion left her by her father Mr Jno Chin and of the legacy lef t h
2 CONC er
2 CONT by her father in Law Mr Jno Stretchley she the sd Cathrine having noe
2 CONT other Right or Claims from my estate.
2 CONT Item I give unto my Son in Law Capt Wm Fox all the rest residue &
2 CONT remarnder of what money is of mine in the hands of Mr Tho Ellis of Lon d
2 CONC on
2 CONT Mercht Excepting and Reserved to the use of Edward Audley (was Jno
2 CONT Stretchley's nephew) one hundred pounds Sterling left him by my husban d
2 CONT Mr Jno Stretchley which I will that my sd Son Wm Fox see him paid of t h
2 CONC e
2 CONT sd money in Ellis his&#00063; hands and in case of his death then th e s
2 CONC d hundred
2 CONT pounds I give to my sd son Wm Fox as also all the rest of the money in
2 CONT his the sd Ellis his hands Except what is bereby before bequeathed in
2 CONT full Leiu of and in full Satisfaction of any futher claims or Chalang e t
2 CONC o
2 CONT any other part or parcell of my sd estate.
2 CONT Item I give to my Sister Tomasin Marshall as much black Crap(e) as wil l
2 CONT make her a gown and peticonte.
2 CONT Item I give to my Sister Dorothy Durham one Christian Servt named Anne
2 CONT Buckley or as much Tobbo as will buy a Cervt which be that is my Cxr
2 CONT shall please to lett her have and all the Remander of my cloaths excep t
2 CONT which is before hereby given.
2 CONT Item I give unto my Cousin Mary Dodson as much black crape as will mak e
2 CONT her a mourning suit.
2 CONT Item I give and bequeath unto my Son Rawleigh Chin all my money in the
2 CONT hands of Mr Jno Pemberton Mercht in Liverpool and all my Slaves Servts
2 CONT Cattle sheep hoggs horses and mares and all and singular the rest resi d
2 CONC ue
2 CONT and Remarndr of my sd estate of what nature or quality soever or
2 CONT wheresoever and of this my last will and Testamt do Constitute and
2 CONT appoint my Son Rawleigh Chinn my whole and sole Exr Revoking all other
2 CONT wills by me herretofore make and doe publish and declare this to be my
2 CONT last will and Testamt in witness whereof I here unto put my hand & sea l
2 CONT the 29th day of August 1701 signed sealed and published in presence of
2 CONT Joseph Tayloe Signed Alice Stretchley
2 CONT (the seal)
2 CONT Lewis Pugh
2 CONT David Smith
2 CONT Probare fuit etc.
2 CONT (proved by three witnesses)
2 CONT 8 October 1701
2 CONT Jos Tayloe Cl.
