1 NOTE  Obituary(Parsons Advocate)
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles M. Hebb was born July 8, 1871 and departed this life, April 14 , 1
2 CONC 914. He was the eldest son of Thomas F. and Lavina S. Hebb and wa s bor
2 CONC n in Tucker county near St. George. In early boyhood he attende d the A
2 CONC cademy at St. George and, afterward graduated at the Mountain S tate Bu
2 CONC siness College, of Parkersburg W. Virginia. Some years ago he w as conv
2 CONC erted under the ministry of Evangelist Blake, and united with t he M.E. c
2 CONC hurch of Parsons, during the pastorate of Rev. H. E. Friend a nd remain
2 CONC ed in the church until his death. He was well known generall y througho
2 CONC ut the county and his business integrity and ability was unq uestioned. h
2 CONC e was a true friend. For a number of years he was a patien t sufferer a
2 CONC nd never seemed gloomy, but always possessed of cheerful o ptimism. The f
2 CONC uneral took place at the M.E. Church in Parsons by Rev . P.Z. Musgrave a
2 CONC ssisted by J. W. Bedford a former pastor, and was att ended by a large n
2 CONC umber of people. He has only gone to join his love d ones who have gone b
2 CONC efore and to wait for those who shall follow aft er.
1 BIRT
2 DATE 8 JUL 1871
2 PLAC Tucker, West Virginia, USA
1 DEAT
2 DATE 14 APR 1914
2 PLAC Tucker, West Virginia, USA
