1 NOTE  TAKEN FROM THE BACK COVER OF "THE BEST OF HERMAN HEBB"
2 CONT
2 CONT My father being a timberman or as they say in the hills "woodhick" w e m
2 CONC oved around alot            when I was very young, following the wo rk o
2 CONC f cutting timber.
2 CONT I was born in the early part of the twentieth century at William, tuck e
2 CONC r County, west Virginia.
2 CONT At one year of age we moved to Leadmine, and at three to Location Road ; f
2 CONC rom there to           Sugarlands in 1917, from there to Parsons i n 19
2 CONC 20. My formal years of education started in           second grad e in t
2 CONC he Old Graded School on River Street and continued until I gradu ated f
2 CONC rom           Blackfork District High School, better known as Pa rsons H
2 CONC igh School in 1931.
2 CONT I enlisted in the United States Navy on August 3, 1931 as apprentice s e
2 CONC aman and continued on           active duty in the navy until Octobe r 1
2 CONC , 1956, retiring as lieutenant commander USN.
2 CONT Although I've stretched my theoretical umbilical chord a few times aro u
2 CONC nd the world it was           never cut. Today I live in Florida, bu t H
2 CONC OME will always be Tucker County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Herman dedicated the book to his mother Margaret Mason Hebb
2 CONT
2 CONT " Whose unfailing devotion and love for her eight children provided u s w
2 CONC ith the courage and stamina that guided our footsteps through all t he t
2 CONC rials, errors and pleasures that mark our lives. A debt that can n ever b
2 CONC e repaid no matter how hard we try.
