1 NOTE  He was originally named Robert de Bruce, and to distinguish him from h i
2 CONC s father and grandfather, who had the same name, he is often referre d t
2 CONC o as Robert de Brucce VIII. He is also called Robert the Bruce. Bru ce d
2 CONC efeated the English in 1314, twice invaded England and in 1323 con clud
2 CONC ed with King Edward II of England a truce for 13 years. After th e acce
2 CONC ssion of King Edward III in 1327, war again broke out and the Sc ots we
2 CONC re again victorious. In 1328 they secured a treaty recognizing t he ind
2 CONC ependence of Scotland and the right of Bruce to the throne. In h is lat
2 CONC er years Bruce was stricken with leprosy and lived in seclusio n at Car
2 CONC doss Castle, on the northern shore of the Firth of Clyde, wher e he die
2 CONC d. He was succeeded by his son, David II. Bruce's nephew, Robe rt II, w
2 CONC ho succeeded David, was the first king of the Stuart house o f English o
2 CONC f English and Scottish royalty.
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1274
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1329
