2 DATE 2 NOV 2019
1 NOTE  !SOURCES: Linn Ford Saunders oral history; copies of family letters an d b
2 CONC ibles in my posession (DWGarner); burial per Margaret Ford Hall.
2 CONT
2 CONT Suzanne Ford Saunders - my Grandmother - Linn Ford Saunders had told m e t
2 CONC hat he was the state superindendent of schools in West Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT George attended the rural schools in his district and Fairmont State N o
2 CONC rmal School; A.B., West Virginia State University, 1892 and LL. B., 1 8
2 CONC 96.
2 CONT He had a commendable military career. He was a cadet at West Virgini a U
2 CONC niversity, 1887-92, graduating first lieutenant, a captain in the S eco
2 CONC nd Infantry of West Virginia National Guard, 1911, a major in the A dju
2 CONC tant General's Department, 1914. He then resigned major's commissio n, 1
2 CONC 916, to accept a commission of captain in the Second West Virgini a Inf
2 CONC antry; and answered the call for Mexican Border service, April 19 17, w
2 CONC ith the thirty-eighth division; discharged April 25, 1919. He ser ved f
2 CONC rom 1917 to 1919 during the World War, saw six months service ove rseas i
2 CONC n command of Company B, 258th Infantry, Nineteenth Division, wh ich was o
2 CONC n duty at Stenay when the Armistice was signed. He then accom panied th
2 CONC is division as part of the Army of Occupation to the Valley o f the Mos
2 CONC elle and later transferred to the Thirty-seventh Division fo r homecomi
2 CONC ng commanding Company M, 145th Infantry.
2 CONT He was a Republican Mason (Knight Templar), and Methodist. He was als o a
2 CONC n Honorary member of Spanish War Veterans; American Legion; Disable d W
2 CONC ar Veterans; Veterans of Foreign Wars, Sigma Chi, and Scabbard an d Bla
2 CONC de.
2 CONT
2 CONT He then had a long and distinguished career as an educator in West Vir g
2 CONC inia.
2 CONT 	Has been principal of the Terra Alta graded schools, Preston County
2 CONT 	Principal of the Grafton High School
2 CONT 	Principal of Concord Normal School
2 CONT 	Head of the Department of Economics and American History, Marshall C o
2 CONC llege
2 CONT 	Superintendent of Bluefield Schools
2 CONT 	Superintendent of Brown's Creek District Schools in McDowell County
2 CONT 	Superintendent of the Dunbar Schools.
2 CONT 	He was elected Superintendent of Free Schools in 1920 for all of Wes t V
2 CONC irginia; re-elected in 1924. President of the West Virginia State E duc
2 CONC ation Association in 1921.
2 CONT
2 CONT from pg. 250 History of Tucker Co, -Fansler
