2 CONT Maud Marshall, died 27 March 1248, daughter and eventual coheiress ofW i
2 CONC lliam Marshall, Earl of Pembroke, by his wife Isabel de Clare, Counte s
2 CONC sof Pembroke.  [Magna Charta Sureties]
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT He [William de Warenne] married, 1stly, Maud. He married, 2ndly, befor e
2 CONC 13 October 1225, Maud, widow of Hugh (BIGOD), EARL OF NORFOLK, daught e
2 CONC rand (after the death s.p. of her 5 brothers) coheir of William (MARS H
2 CONC AL),4th EARL OF PEMBROKE, by Isabel, daughter and (after her brother' s d
2 CONC eathin childhood) heir of Richard (FITZGILBERT), 2nd EARL OF PEMBRO KE. H
2 CONC edied 27 May 1240 in London and was buried before the high alta r in Le
2 CONC wesPriory. Maud died between 1 and 7 April 1248.  [Complete Pee rageXII
2 CONC /1:500-03, (transcribed by Dave Utzinger)]
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Maud Marshal m. 1st to Hugh Bigod, Earl of Norfolk; 2ndly, to Willia m d
2 CONC eWarren, Earl of Surrey; and 3rdly, to Walde de Dunstanville. Thi s lad
2 CONC y,upon the decease of her youngest brother, Anselm, Earl of Pembr oke, s
2 CONC .p., in 1245, and the division of the estates, obtained as her s hare t
2 CONC hemanor of Hempsted-Marshall, in Berks, with the office of marsh al ofE
2 CONC ngland, which was inherited by her son Roger Bigod, 4th Earl o f Norfol
2 CONC k,and surrendered to the crown by her grandson, Rogert Bigod , 5th Earl o
2 CONC fNorfolk. Maud, Countess of Norfolk, had likewise the mano rs of Chepst
2 CONC owand Carlogh. [Sir Bernard Burke, Dormant, Abeyant, Forfe ited, and Ex
2 CONC tinctPeerages, Burke's Peerage, Ltd., London, 1883, p. 358 , Marshal, E
2 CONC arls ofPembroke]
