2 CONT Titles 8th Earl of Arundel
2 CONT
2 CONT EDMUND FITZ ALAN, Earl of Arundel, son and heir, born 1 May 1285, in t h
2 CONC eCastle of Marlborough. His wardship was obtained by John, Earl of Su r
2 CONC reyand Sussex, whose granddaughter he married. He was knighted, wit h E
2 CONC dward,the King's son, and many others, 22 May 1306. On 9 November 1 306 h
2 CONC e wassummoned to Parliament as Earl of Arundel, and took part i n the S
2 CONC cottishwars of that year. On 25 February 1307/8 he officiated a s Pince
2 CONC rna at thecoronation of Edward II. In 1316 he was Captain Gener al nort
2 CONC h of theTrent. For a long time he was in opposition to the King , and w
2 CONC as violentagainst Piers
2 CONT Gaveston, who had beaten him in a tournament. However in 1321 he chang e
2 CONC d
2 CONT sides, and married his first son to a daughter of Hugh le Despenser,be i
2 CONC ng
2 CONT thereafter one of the few nobles who adhered to the King. In 1323 he w a
2 CONC s
2 CONT Chief Justiciar of North and South Wales. Warden of the Welsh Marches1 3
2 CONC 25. Having been captured in Shropshire by the Queen's party, he was,w i
2 CONC thout trial, beheaded at Hereford, 17 November 1326 in his 42nd year. H
2 CONC e was subsequently attainted, when his estates and honours becameforf e
2 CONC ited. His widow [who, in her issue was, in 1347, sole heir of herbrot h
2 CONC er John, Earl of Surrey and Sussex, and consequently of the greatfami l
2 CONC y of Warenne] was
2 CONT living 1330, but died before 23 May 1338. Source CP 1:241-2
