2 CONT A miracle which is said to have happened after the death of [Richard d e
2 CONC Wych, Bishop of Chichester, b. 1197-d. 1253] relates to a young son o f
2 CONC the Countess of Arundel--a daughter of one of the De Warennes--who la y
2 CONC very ill in Lewes Castle. At last all appeared to be over and the bod y
2 CONC was left unattended; but later a girl named Johanna entered, and knel t
2 CONC and prayed to St. Richard de Wych for the soul of the boy, whoimmedia t
2 CONC ely gave signs of life and ultimately recovered.
