2 CONT Richard II by writs directed "Johnann de Arundel", whereby he may be h e
2 CONC ldto have become Lord Arundel.  He was Marshall of England in that sa m
2 CONC eyear, 1377, and also April 9, 1378.  Being in command of a navalexpe d
2 CONC ition in aid of the Duke of Brittany, he defeated the French Fleetof f t
2 CONC he coast of Cornwall, but later, December 15, 1379, wrecked anddrow ned i
2 CONC n the Irish Sea.  He was buried in Lewes Priory.  Will datedNovem ber 1
2 CONC 6, 1379.
