1 NOTE  11th Earl Arundel
2 CONT Cause of Death:Beheaded
2 CONT
2 CONT RICHARD FITZ ALAN, Earl of Arundel, and Earl of Surrey, son and heir , b
2 CONC y2nd wife, born in 1346. He was bearer of the Crown at the coronati on o
2 CONC fRichard II, 16 July 1377, was a member of the Council, and was ma deAd
2 CONC miral of the West and South, 1377, and subsequently, 1386, of allE ngla
2 CONC nd. K.G., distinguished himself in the French Wars, and "won abril lian
2 CONC t naval victory over the French, Spanish, & Flemish fleets offMarg ate i
2 CONC n 24 March 1387"; and was made Governor of Brest in 1388, beingon e of t
2 CONC he five Lords Appellant in  the Parliament of that year.
2 CONT
2 CONT Together with the Duke of Gloucester he later took an active part in t h
2 CONC eopposition to King Richard, who, in 1388, was entirely in that Duke' s
2 CONC power. In 1394 he obtained a pardon for all political offences, but w a
2 CONC streacherously seized, 12 July 1397, tried at Westminster, and behead e
2 CONC d atCheapside on 21 September 1397.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married [contract dated 28 September, Papal dispensation, the samem o
2 CONC nth, 1359] Elizabeth, daughter of William [Bohun], Earl of Northampto n
2 CONC ,by Elizabeth, daughter of Bartholomew Badlesmere. She died 3 April 1 3
2 CONC 85,and was buried at Lewes.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 2ndly [without Royal license, for which he was fined 500mar k
2 CONC s], 15 August 1390, Philippe, widow of John Hastings, and daughter of E
2 CONC dmund [Mortimer], Earl of March, by Philippe, daughter and heir ofLio n
2 CONC el, Duke of Clarence.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was buried at Austin Friars', in Bread Street, London, and, havingb e
2 CONC en attainted, all his honors were forfeited. His widow [by whom he ha d
2 CONC no issue] was born 21 November 1375, at Ludlow, married 3rdly, afterA p
2 CONC ril 1398, Thomas [Poynings], Lord St. John of Basing, and died 24Sept e
2 CONC mber 1401, at Halnaker, Sussex, being buried at Boxgrove.
