2 CONT
2 CONT BARONY OF STANLEY
2 CONT
2 CONT I. 1. THOMAS STANLEY, of Lathom and Knowsley, Lancs, son and heir. H e w
2 CONC as born in or before 1405. In 1430/1 he was a knight, and Lieutenan t o
2 CONC f Ireland; and so continued (described as King's knight) until 9 No vem
2 CONC ber 1436, or later. On 6 December 1437 he was appointed constable o f C
2 CONC hester Castle; and on 26 April 1439 he was granted, during good beh avi
2 CONC our, the offices of Controller of the Household, Chamberlain of Nor th W
2 CONC ales, and (with another) Forester of Macclesfield. On 1 December 1 443 h
2 CONC e, with the Earl of Suffolk, had a grant in survivorship of the o ffice o
2 CONC f justice of the cos. of Chester and Flint and of North Wales ; and on 1
2 CONC 1 December 1448, with the same, had a grant of the office o f Chief Ste
2 CONC ward of the Duchy of Lancaster. On 2 April 1450 he was appo inted with o
2 CONC thers to be warden of Calais, &c. In 1451 the Commons peti tioned for h
2 CONC is removal from the Court. In 1455 he is described as Thom as Stanley, k
2 CONC night, Lord Stanley, the King's Chamberlain. He was summo ned to Parlia
2 CONC ment 15 January 1455/6 by writ directed Thome Stanley mil iti domino de S
2 CONC tanley, whereby he is held to have become LORD STANLEY . Nominated K.G. b
2 CONC efore 13 May, installed 14 May 1457. He married. Joa n, daughter and co
2 CONC heir of Sir Robert GOUSHILL of Hoveringham, Notts, b y Elizabeth, widow o
2 CONC f (i) Sir William DE MONTAGU and (ii) Thomas (DE M OWBRAY), 1st DUKE OF N
2 CONC ORFOLK, daughter of Richard (FITZALAN), EARL O F ARUNDEL. He died 11 Fe
2 CONC bruary 1458/9. Joan survived him.  [CP 12[1]:2 50-1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Name Suffix:<NSFX> K.B., Lord Stanley of Lathom & Knowsley, K.G.
2 CONT Name Prefix:< NPFX> Sir
