1 NOTE  BARONY OF GREY OF CODNOR (VII)
2 CONT
2 CONT SIR HENRY (GREY), LORD GREY (of Codnor), son and heir, was aged 9 at h i
2 CONC s father's death. On 8 February 1451/2 his wardship was granted to Jo h
2 CONC n (Beaumont), Viscount Beaumont, for 400 marks. He was summoned to Pa r
2 CONC liament from 9 October 1459 to 14 October 1495, by writs directed Hen r
2 CONC ico Grey chivaler. He was with Queen Margaret at the Battle of St. Al b
2 CONC ans, 1460. On 21 October 1463 he had a grant to himself, deputies an d a
2 CONC ssigns of power and authority to labour, by the conning of philosop hy t
2 CONC he transmutation of metals at his own cost, but he should answer t o th
2 CONC e King if any profit grew. On 12 March 1472/3 he had a grant for 4 0 ye
2 CONC ars of land in the north of Ireland and was appointed steward of a ll t
2 CONC he King's castles, &c., belonging to the Earl of Ulster. He ha d a gene
2 CONC ral pardon, 30 May 1480, for all offences committed prior to 2 4 May. H
2 CONC e was present, 6 July 1483, at the Coronation of Richard III , who on 1
2 CONC 8 May 1484 granted to him and his heirs male, for his good s ervice aga
2 CONC inst the rebels, the manors or lordships of Oakham, Langha m and Exton, R
2 CONC utland, and Hengrave, Haverhill, and Hersham, Suffolk. A t the creation o
2 CONC f the Duke of York (1494) the King, by advice of his l ords, ordained t
2 CONC he Lord Grey to go before the Lord Clifford.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, 1stly, shortly after 31 August 1454, Catherine, daughter o f S
2 CONC ir Thomas STRANGWAYS, by Catherine, daughter of Ralph (NEVILLE), EA RL O
2 CONC F WESTMORLAND, and widow of John (MOWBRAY), DUKE OF NORFOLK. He ma rrie
2 CONC d, 2ndly, in or before 1458/9, Margaret, one of the 3 daughters o f Sir R
2 CONC alph Moton. He married, 3rdly, in or after 1486, and before 5 M ay 1492
2 CONC , Catherine, widow of Sir William BERKELEY, of Beverston, Count y Glouc
2 CONC ester, and daughter, as is stated, of William (STOURTON), LOR D STOURTO
2 CONC N. He died s.p. legitimate 18 April 1495. He desired burial i n the cha
2 CONC ncel of Our Lady in the Friars of Aylesford. To his widow h e bequeathe
2 CONC d for her jointure half his goods, Aylesford and Hoo Hundre ds in Kent, G
2 CONC rays Thurrock in Essex, Bytham Park, Stocking and South W itham in Linc
2 CONC olnshire, Sapcote and £3 in County Leicester, and Langwyn te Basset in C
2 CONC ounty Derby.
2 CONT
2 CONT His coheirs were his 3 aunts (or their descendants), daughters of Rich a
2 CONC rd (Grey), 4th Lord Grey (of Codnor). (1) Elizabeth, wife of Sir Joh n Z
2 CONC ouche of Bulwick, County Northampton, younger son of William, 4th L ord Z
2 CONC ouche. This Sir John Zouche purchased from the last Lord the cast le an
2 CONC d manor of Codnor with other manors in cos. Derby and Notts in re versi
2 CONC on after the death of Catherine wife of the said last Lord. He wa s fat
2 CONC her of another Sir John Zouche, who married a daughter of Sir Hen ry Wi
2 CONC lloughby. The counterpart of an indenture dated 21 July 1501 reci tes t
2 CONC hat Henry, Lord Grey, willed the manor and castle of Codnor, &c. , shou
2 CONC ld be sold to the King to the use of his son Henry, Duke of York , for £
2 CONC 1,000, and it was therefore arranged that the King before 30 No vember c
2 CONC oming should pay the £1,000. Before 3 August 1509 it was foun d that th
2 CONC e original sale between Henry, Lord Grey of Codnor, and Joh n Zouche, o
2 CONC f Bulwick, father of John Zouche [then living], was genuin e and Codnor
2 CONC , &c., were sold to the above Henry Willoughby and John Zo uche for £1,
2 CONC 400. [2] Eleanor, wife of Sir Thomas Newport, of High Erca ll, Salop. (
2 CONC 3) Lucy, wife of Sir Rowland Lenthall, of Lenthall and Ham pton Court, C
2 CONC ounty Hereford.
2 CONT
2 CONT Among their representatives any hereditary Barony which may be suppose d t
2 CONC o have been created by the writ of 1299 appears to be in abeyance . [Co
2 CONC mplete Peerage VI:130-3, XIV:352-3, (transcribed by Dave Utzinger )]
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: The identification of Henry's 2nd wife as Margaret, daughter o f R
2 CONC alph Moton (originally identified only as "Margaret", but added t o the O
2 CONC riginal CP by the correction in Volume XIV), is proven wrong b y the po
2 CONC sting below of Chris Phillips to soc.genealogy.medieval, and i s correc
2 CONC ted to be Margaret Stanley by a later posting by Kerrie Rafter .
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The following is excerpted from a posting by Chris Phillips to soc.gen e
2 CONC alogy.medieval, 13 Oct 2002:
2 CONT
2 CONT Unfortunately Reginald's [Somehow Reginald Moton became known as Ralph .
2 CONC ] death is in the period not yet covered by the published abstracts o f i
2 CONC nquisitions post mortem, but some details are given in Nichols' His tor
2 CONC y of Leicestershire (vol. 4, pp. 995, 996; Thurleston). This says t hat i
2 CONC n 1445 it was found that Reginald Moton died seised (as of the ri ght o
2 CONC f Margaret his wife) of the manor of Thurleston, and divers land s at W
2 CONC igston Magna - the manor had been settled on Reginald, Margare t and th
2 CONC eir lawful issue - "and that Anne and Elizabeth Moton were th e daughte
2 CONC rs and next heirs of Reginald Moton aforesaid" [citing Esch . 24 Hen. V
2 CONC I. dors. 38].
2 CONT
2 CONT This seems to be pretty clear evidence that Reginald Moton had only tw o d
2 CONC aughters, and that the reference in the account has been misinterpr ete
2 CONC d, or is just plain wrong (although apparently only about 15 year s aft
2 CONC er his death, it names the man as Ralph rather than Reginald, cal ls hi
2 CONC m a knight - which he is not called by either the visitation pedi gree o
2 CONC r Nichols' notes from the inquisition - and doesn't know the for enames o
2 CONC f any of the supposed husbands).
2 CONT
2 CONT STANLEY SOLUTION
2 CONT
2 CONT That leaves Ormerod's old identification of Margaret as the daughter o f L
2 CONC ord Stanley. Unfortunately the details are given in a pedigree, wit hou
2 CONC t the sources being cited, except that Ormerod does refer to a disp ens
2 CONC ation dated 23 January 1459 for Margaret's remarriage to John Butle r, d
2 CONC escribed in a footnote as "the letters of the bishop" (I couldn' t find a
2 CONC ny mention of this in the published abstracts from the papal r egisters
2 CONC ).
2 CONT
2 CONT Ormerod also refers to a lost tomb, formerly in the Troutbeck chapel i n S
2 CONC t Mary's church, Chester, which he suggests was erected by Margaret 's 1
2 CONC st husband Sir William, in memory of his grandfather. Among the ar ms o
2 CONC n this tomb were "Troutbeck impaling Stanley; (the coat of Stanle y imp
2 CONC aled wih Latham, and the arms of Man in chief)". I presume that w ould b
2 CONC e right for Lord Stanley, her suggested father.
2 CONT
2 CONT So Ormerod's identification is lacking in evidence, but the Moton alte r
2 CONC native appears definitely wrong.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The following is excerpted from a posting by Kerrie Rafter to soc.gene a
2 CONC logy.medieval, 13 Oct 2002:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Boteler died on 26 Feb 1462-3. Margaret afterwards married He n
2 CONC ry, lord Grey of Codnor, & died about 1481 [Beaumont, Lords of Warrin g
2 CONC ton (Chetham Soc.) 294, 300;Chester Visit. of 1580 (Harl. Soc) 223]
2 CONT
2 CONT The tomb formerly by the south wall near the east end of the Troutbec k c
2 CONC hapel in St Mary's Chester, was that of Sir William, judging by th e ar
2 CONC ms displayed on it. On the slab were the figures of a knight & hi s wif
2 CONC e, & below, on the end wall o the tomb, were the arms of Troutbec k and S
2 CONC tanley.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the side wall were the following arms, showing the family alliances ;
2 CONT 1. Troutbeck impaling Butler of Bewsey
2 CONT 2. Butler impaling Troutbeck
2 CONT 3. Brereton
2 CONT 4. Troutbeck, impaling Holes.
2 CONT The other side & end of the tomb seem to have been against the walls o f t
2 CONC he
2 CONT chapel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kerrie Rafter
2 CONT Warwick.Qld
2 CONT Australia
2 CONT kerrie@halenet.com.au
