2 CONT Cause of Death Murdered by a servant after Battle of Shrewsbury
2 CONT
2 CONT I believe that Sir Robert Goushill fought on the royal side, not there b
2 CONC el side, at the Battle of Shrewsbury. He had been a retainer of Thoma s
2 CONC Mowbray, Duke of Norfolk; was out of favor with Richard II afterNorfo l
2 CONC k's exile in 1398; was rehabilitated as a result of the Lancastrianus u
2 CONC rpation, and married Norfolk's widow. Thus his loyalties were strongl y
2 CONC Lancastrian in 1403. See Roskell, History of Parliament 3:217; E.B.Pr i
2 CONC estley, The Battle of Shrewsbury 1403 (1979) p. 16.
