2 CONC g. John helped Edward III break the power of Mortimer and shut the"sh e
2 CONC -wolf" from France in Framlingham Castle. In 1336 Edward constitutedJ o
2 CONC hn as Admiral and Captain of the King's navy from the mouth of theTha m
2 CONC es northward and was made a knight-banneret.
2 CONT
2 CONT John was considered a gallant Navy man. He ferried Edwards victoriousa r
2 CONC mies into France and harried the French coasts by landing men and"lay i
2 CONC ng waste the county with fire and sword". When John left the Navy heb e
2 CONC came Sheriff of Norfolk in 1345. John and wife Alice lived mainly int h
2 CONC e Manor of Fersfield which was constructed by his grandfather and whi c
2 CONC hremained in the Howard family for centuries. John attended the funer a
2 CONC l ofhis oldest son Robert in 1388 and created several memorials tha t l
2 CONC asted.
