1 NOTE  In 1306 John obtained the wardship of the lands and thus became the he i
2 CONC rof John de Crokefale in Norfolk. He was summoned by King Edward to h i
2 CONC scoronation at Westminster. John distinguished himself in the wars of G
2 CONC ascony and Scotland. The terrible overthrow of the English forces atB a
2 CONC nnockburn disgusted John so he contented himself with becoming Sherif f
2 CONC .He was knighted and was Sheriff of both Norfolk and Suffolk for 13 y e
2 CONC ars.He did raise troops for Edward II and III. For a short period Joh n w
2 CONC asGovernor of Norwich. Certainly the influence of the parents of hi s w
2 CONC ifehelped in Johns eminence. With Joan's inheritance, they became t her
2 CONC ichest landowners in western Norfolk. Joan was in many ways the mor ein
2 CONC fluential.
