1 NOTE  Robert and his wife Margaret caused the merger of the fortunes of theg r
2 CONC eat families, Mowbray's, Howard's, Fitzalan, and Berkeley's. SinceRob e
2 CONC rt died at about the same time as his father, his son actually merged t
2 CONC he properties.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert was known as a valiant fighter whether on the land or sea. Hese r
2 CONC ved under King Henry V in France and fought at Agincourt. He commande d
2 CONC the English fleet and with 3,000 mariners of East Anglia, he sailed o u
2 CONC r oLowestoft, landed below Calais and ravaged the French coasts. He g a
2 CONC inedthe affection of Harry of Monmouth who led him to his marriage t o L
2 CONC adyMargaret Mowbray, daughter of one of the proudest houses in Engl and
2 CONC .Margaret's brother John was a companion in arms to Robert.
