2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella Despenser's marriage to FitzAlan was later annulled on thepet i
2 CONC tion of her husband, who claimed that he had been coerced into theuni o
2 CONC n for political reasons (i.e., her father's ambition). The son andtw o d
2 CONC aughters that had been born to them were specifically bastardized b yth
2 CONC e annulment decree. I can't remember offhand if either of the daugh ter
2 CONC sever married, but the son did, and his descendants used the surnam eAr
2 CONC undell (See CP s.v. "Arundel" for particulars on this annulment an d th
2 CONC e3 children).
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: 9 FEB 1320/21 in King's Chapel, Havering-atte-Bower
2 CONT Marriage fact: in annulled on petition of husband, claiming coercion
