2 CONT
2 CONT OCCUPATION:  He became in monk later in life.Roger de Beaumont; Seigne u
2 CONC r (feudal Lord) of Beaumont, Pontaudemer, Brionne and Vatteville, Nor m
2 CONC andy; married Adeline, sister of Hugh Count of Meulan and daughter b y h
2 CONC is 1st wife of Waleran Count of Meulan.  [Burke's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The well-known Roger de Beaumont held Sturminster Marshal, Dorset, i n 1
2 CONC 086; it descended to the counts of Meulan through Roger's eldest so n, R
2 CONC obert count of Meulan.  That Roger took his name from Beaumont i s a pa
2 CONC rt of the general history of Normandy.  It follows that Roger' s descen
2 CONC dants, the counts of Meulan, the Earls of Leicester, and the E arls of W
2 CONC arwick, all derive from Beaumont-le-Roger.  [The Origins of S ome Anglo
2 CONC -Norman Families][From "The Origins of Some Anglo-Norman Fami lies"]The w
2 CONC ell-known Roger de Beaumont held Sturminster Marshal, Dorse t, in 1086; i
2 CONC t descended to the counts of Meulan through Roger's eldes t son, Robert c
2 CONC ount of Meulan.  That Roger took his name from Beaumon t is a part of t
2 CONC he general history of Normandy.  It follows that Roger 's descendants, t
2 CONC he counts of Meulan, the earls of Leicester, and th e earls of Warwick, a
2 CONC ll derive from Beaumont-le-Roger.
2 CONT
