1 NOTE  OCCUPATION:  King 1087-1100 (UNMARRIED)MISC: Ruled 1087-1100, Never Ma r
2 CONC riedReigned 1087-1100. His harsh rule aroused baronial and acclesiast i
2 CONC cal opposition, notably from Anselm, Archbishop of Canterbury. He mad e s
2 CONC everal attempts to recover Normandy from his elder brother Robert a nd w
2 CONC as killed by an arrow while hunting. He may have been assasinate d by o
2 CONC rder of his younger bother who became Henry I. Had Red Hair. H e had ve
2 CONC ry little time for religion and presided over a liberal cour t but trea
2 CONC ted his subjects brutally.He was reluctant to fill church va cancies an
2 CONC d waited 4 years to appoint Anselm.
