2 CONC ing of England, she chose to be buried beside her mother at Cae n under a
2 CONC n inscription 'Adela, filia regis'. She was always the Conque ror's dau
2 CONC ghter. [Sources: Who's Who in Early Medieval England, Christo pher Tyer
2 CONC man, Shepheard-Walwyn, Ltd., London, 1996; EncyclopSia Britan nica CD, 1
2 CONC 997]
2 CONT
2 CONT *********
