2 GIVN Sibella (Sibyl) de
2 SURN Corbet
1 SEX F
1 _UID EF061E531E714E96B356B2E4BCF3C9DCCC83
1 _AMTID 162143283686:1030:164657654
1 CHAN
2 DATE 2 NOV 2019
1 NOTE  OCCUPATION:  Mistress of Henry I; Lady of Alcester, County Warwick an d o
2 CONC f Pontesbury and Woodcote, County SalopCorbet, mistress of Henry I , la
2 CONC dy of Alcester, County Warwick and of Pontesbury and Woodcote, Cou nty S
2 CONC alop (by Henry I she was mother of Reginald Fitz Roy, Earl of Cor nwall
2 CONC ).  [Ancestral Roots]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The following additional info was supplied by Curt Hofemann, curt_hofe m
2 CONC ann@yahoo.com:
2 CONT
2 CONT no evidence to prove that Henry I married Sibyl [Ref: Sheppard Apr65 p 9
2 CONC 6]
2 CONT
2 CONT It is because of Henry I's personal propensities that we know somethin g o
2 CONC f two Corbet women who occur in the records of this period. his num ero
2 CONC us mistresses Sibyl Corbet, elder daughter of Robert fitz Corbet o f Lo
2 CONC ngden, must have been a favourite since she bore four, possibly fi ve, o
2 CONC f Henry's illegitimate children. [Ref: CP XI Appendix D]
2 CONT
2 CONT She had a younger sister Alice. Where, when and how the liaison bega n b
2 CONC etween Henry and Sibyl is a mystery. He had already had children b y va
2 CONC rious mistresses: among the oldest must have been Juliane, who mar ried E
2 CONC ustace de Pacy lord of Breteuil in 1103, and rebelled against he r fath
2 CONC er; and Robert, born of an unknown woman of Caen, who was create d earl o
2 CONC f Gloucester by his father in 1122. [Ref Corbet citing: CP V:6 83: the s
2 CONC uggestion that he was the son of Sibyl Corbet is probably cor rect]
2 CONT
2 CONT The known children by Sibyl Corbet were Rainaud de Dunstanville, his b r
2 CONC other William and sisters Gundred and Rohese; it is also possible, bu t n
2 CONC ot certain, that Sibyl was the mother of the king's illegitimate da ugh
2 CONC ter Sibyl who was married to Alexander after he became king of th e Sco
2 CONC ts in 1107. [Ref: Corbet citing: A.C. Lawrie, Early Scottish Char ters, G
2 CONC lasgow 1905:charter XXXVI to Scone Priory, Alexander I, c. 1120 , witne
2 CONC ssed by Queen Sibyl and her brother William; she died 12 June 1 122 on a
2 CONC n island in Loch Tay to which Alexander granted charter XLVII , to cano
2 CONC ns of Scone]
2 CONT
2 CONT Note 1: Sheppard = Walter Lee Sheppard, Royal Bye-Blows II: The Illegi t
2 CONC imate Royal Offspring from Edward III To Queen Anne, NEHGR vol 21, 19 6
2 CONC 7.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note 2: Corbet = The Corbett Study Group, http://website.lineone.net/~ c
2 CONC orbett_group/First/people.htm
2 CONT specifically: The Anglo Norman Corbets by Barbara Coulton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Regards,
2 CONT Curt
2 CONT
2 CONT **********
