2 CONT [From Burke's Peerage-see source for details]
2 CONT
2 CONT An undoubted Earl of Gloucester, perhaps the first authentic one, at a n
2 CONC y rate after the Conquest, is Robert FitzHamon's son-in-law, anothe r R
2 CONC obert, who was an illegitimate son of Henry I and was so created 11 22. T
2 CONC he Earldom passed to his eldest son, William FitzRobert, and fro m him t
2 CONC o John, later King John and husband from 1189 to 1199 (when h e divorce
2 CONC d her) of Isabel, the youngest of William FitzRobert's thre e daughters
2 CONC .  On John's coming to the throne the title did not merge i n the Crown f
2 CONC or it was not his in his own right but in right of his wi fe.ALIAS: Wil
2 CONC liam FitzRobert Meullent
2 CONT
2 CONT [From Burke's Peerage-see source for details]
2 CONT
2 CONT An undoubted Earl of Gloucester, perhaps the first authentic one, at a n
2 CONC y rate after the Conquest, is Robert FitzHamon's son-in-law, anothe r R
2 CONC obert, who was an illegitimate son of Henry I and was so created 11 22. T
2 CONC he Earldom passed to his eldest son, William FitzRobert, and fro m him t
2 CONC o John, later King John and husband from 1189 to 1199 (when h e divorce
2 CONC d her) of Isabel, the youngest of William FitzRobert's thre e daughters
2 CONC .  On John's coming to the throne the title did not merge i n the Crown f
2 CONC or it was not his in his own right but in right of his wi fe.Alternate n
2 CONC ame found in file: William Fitzrobert Meullent
2 CONT
2 CONT [From Burke's Peerage-see source for details]An undoubted Earl of Glou c
2 CONC ester, perhaps the first authentic one, at any rate after the Conques t
2 CONC , is Robert FitzHamon's son-in-law, another Robert, who was an illegi t
2 CONC imate son of Henry I and was so created 1122. The Earldom passed to h i
2 CONC s eldest son, William FitzRobert, and from him to John, later King Jo h
2 CONC n and husband from 1189 to 1199 (when he divorced her) of Isabel, th e y
2 CONC oungest of William FitzRobert's three daughters.  On John's comin g to t
2 CONC he throne the title did not merge in the Crown for it was not hi s in h
2 CONC is own right but in right of his wife.
2 CONT
