1 NOTE  Nest (who also [in addition to Gerald fitz Walter] had by Stephen, Con s
2 CONC table of Cardigan, a son (Robert fitz Stephen) and by Henry I anothe r s
2 CONC on (Henry, killed 1158, father of Meiler fitz Henry), daughter of R hys a
2 CONC p Tudor Mawr, Prince of South Wales.  [Burke's Peerage, p. 1679]N est (
2 CONC who also [in addition to Gerald fitz Walter] had by Stephen, Cons table o
2 CONC f Cardigan, a son (Robert fitz Stephen) and by Henry I anothe r son (He
2 CONC nry, killed 1158, father of Meiler fitz Henry), daughter of R hys ap Tu
2 CONC dor Mawr, Prince of South Wales.  [Burke's Peerage, p. 1679]N est (who a
2 CONC lso [in addition to Gerald fitz Walter] had by Stephen, Cons table of C
2 CONC ardigan, a son (Robert fitz Stephen) and by Henry I anothe r son (Henry
2 CONC , killed 1158, father of Meiler fitz Henry), daughter of R hys ap Tudor M
2 CONC awr, Prince of South Wales.  [Burke's Peerage, p. 1679]
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT He [Gerald de Windsor] married Nest, daughter of Rhys ap Tudor Mawr, P R
2 CONC INCE OF SOUTH WALES (e). The date of his death is not known, presumab l
2 CONC y before 1136. [Complete Peerage X:10-11, (transcribed by Dave Utzing e
2 CONC r)]
2 CONT
2 CONT (e) In 1106, when Owen ap Cadugan carried her off, two of her sons an d a d
2 CONC aughter by Gerald de Windsor were taken with her, the sons bein g retur
2 CONC ned later to their father.  By Stephen, constable of Cardigan ( query a
2 CONC fter Gerald's death), Nest bore a son, Robert FitzStephen, an d by Henr
2 CONC y I a son Henry (killed 1158), father of Meiler FitzHenry, wh ich Rober
2 CONC t and Meiler were later brothers-in-arms of the Geraldines i n Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT ********
2 CONT
2 CONT Nest (who also [in addition to Gerald fitz Walter] had by Stephen, Con s
2 CONC table of Cardigan, a son (Robert fitz Stephen) and by Henry I anothe r s
2 CONC on (Henry, killed 1158, father of Meiler fitz Henry), daughter of R hys a
2 CONC p Tudor Mawr, Prince of South Wales.  [Burke's Peerage, p. 1679]
2 CONT
2 CONT Known as the most beautiful woman in Wales. She had many lovers. In Ch r
2 CONC istmas 1108 Owain ap Cadwgan of Cardigan came to visit Gerald and Nes t
2 CONC a. He so lusted after her that he, that night, attacked the castle an d c
2 CONC arried her off and had his way with her. This upset Henry I [King o f E
2 CONC ngland] so much that the incident started a war.
2 CONT Source:www.dcs.hull.ac.ukShe was stunningly beautiful, called the Hele n o
2 CONC f Wales. She was the daughter of the last king of independent Deheu bar
2 CONC th, she was the mistress of Henry I, king of England,and had a so n by h
2 CONC im Robert DeCarn, Earl of Dorchester and Gloucester. Henry I too k the t
2 CONC hrone away from his brother in 1100. She was the wife of Geral d de Win
2 CONC dsor,Constable of Pembroke, she was romantically abducted by O wain ap C
2 CONC adwgan,son of the Prince of Powys, and is generally suppose d to have h
2 CONC ad any number of other romantic liaisons. She was the found er of more d
2 CONC ynasties than is polite to mention. Thousands of Welsh chi ldren today a
2 CONC re still refered to as Nest in her honour.
2 CONT
2 CONT ************
