2 CONT OCCUPATION:  Duke of Normandy 1026-1028
2 CONT
2 CONT MARRIAGE:  All children EXCEPT for Nicholas, Abbot of St. Owen who ill e
2 CONC g. by a mistress.
2 CONT
2 CONT DEATH:  Poisoned by his brother Robert.Richard II, by name RICHARD, Fr e
2 CONC nch RICHARD le BON (d. 1026/27), duke of Normandy (996-1026/27), so n o
2 CONC f Richard I the Fearless. He held his own against a peasant insurre cti
2 CONC on, helped Robert II of France against the duchy of Burgundy, and r epe
2 CONC lled an English attack on the Cotentin Peninsula that was led by th e A
2 CONC nglo-Saxon king Ethelred II the Unready. He also pursued a reform o f t
2 CONC he Norman monasteries. [Encyclopaedia Britannica CD '97]
2 CONT
2 CONT *******
