2 CONT Raoul/Rudolf/Ralph, count of Ivry, is the uterine brother of Richar d I o
2 CONC f Normandy, son of William. ("This was given by Dudo based on inf ormat
2 CONC ion supplied to him by Raoul himself, so is perfectly reliable" , as To
2 CONC dd's mentioned.)  But my understanding has always been that Rao ul was t
2 CONC he son of Sprota/Esporta de Bretagne/Senlis not by William Lon gsword b
2 CONC ut by Asperling/Esperlingus/Eperling. [Ref: Christopher Nash m essage t
2 CONC o Gen-Medieval 15 Apr 2002 discussing an error in KSB Keats-Ro han's Do
2 CONC mesday People.  TAF (Todd A Farmerie) in response confirmed th e above] n
2 CONC ote: she was NOT de Senlis and as far as "de Bretagne" see b elow... Cu
2 CONC rt
2 CONT
2 CONT While this speculation is certainly possible, the alternative is likew i
2 CONC se possible, that being that she was just some cute looking Breton pe a
2 CONC sant that William took a liking to. That, however, provides no opport u
2 CONC nity for further genealogical research, so tends to pale in compariso n t
2 CONC o the possibility of attaching her to some noble house. My gut reac tio
2 CONC n is that, considering her son Ralph (d'Ivry) was one of the main s our
2 CONC ces of the norman historian Dudo, yet no such important connectio n was m
2 CONC entioned, she likely did not have any hereditary recomendation s (sic) w
2 CONC hen chosen by Longsword. [Ref: TAF 9 Dec 2002]
2 CONT
2 CONT Regards,
2 CONT Curt
2 CONT
2 CONT ************
