1 NOTE  MISC:  Geoffrey, count of Anjou, sat among the barons wearing a tuni c o
2 CONC f course grey cloth that the French call grising but which Angevin s ca
2 CONC ll borrel.  The miller, who had been summoned by the king for thi s exp
2 CONC ress purpose, looked at the count and recognized his immediate .  As he k
2 CONC nelt, he caught hold of the count's tunic and said to the ki ng and the r
2 CONC est of those assembled,  "This man, who wears a grey tunic , restored o
2 CONC ur honour when he slew Ethelulf the Dane and struck fear i nto their ar
2 CONC my."  The king decreed that henceforth Geoffrey should b e called 'Grey
2 CONC gown', and all present gave their assent.  Nickname als o "Greygown"[SU
2 CONC SANNA KEENE.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT Rec'd in requital of his gallant services against the Emperor Otto th e g
2 CONC rant from King Robert of the dignified office of Seneschal of Franc e.
