1 NOTE  Mauger, Count of Corbeil, in right of his wife; married Germaine, daug h
2 CONC ter and heir of Albert, Count of Corbeil, and had [Hamon, Count of Co r
2 CONC beil], with an elder son (William, dsp a monk in the Abbey of St. Mau r
2 CONC ).  [Burke's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT Note the above puts the descendancy through William in doubt.  cours e b
2 CONC eing an elder son, he could have been Count at least for a while, a nd m
2 CONC aybe had illegitimate children.  Though they would not be Counts.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the ancestry of the Grenville's and parents of Mauger, Count of Cor b
2 CONC eil, their ancestor:
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard I, Duke of Normandy (ggf through his eldest son of Robert II ( T
2 CONC he Devil), Duke of Normandy, who was in turn father by his mistress H a
2 CONC rlette/Harlot of William I (The Conqueror); b 933; married 2nd his fo r
2 CONC mer mistress Gunnor and died 20 Nov 996, leaving [Mauger].  [Burke' s P
2 CONC eerage, p. 1603]
2 CONT
