2 CONT Henry de Percy, 2nd Lord (Baron) Percy; born 6 Feb 1300/1&#00063;; gra n
2 CONC tedcustody of Alnwick Castle 1318, custodian of Scarborough Castle 13 2
2 CONC 1-24,knighted 1322, Keeper of the coast: Yorks 1324 and Northumberlan d 1
2 CONC 325,Keeper of the Peace Northumberland 1325, sided with Queen Isabe lla
2 CONC against her husband Edward II's last favourites the Despensers 1326 ,Ke
2 CONC eper of Skipton Castle, chief commissioner to monitor observance o f th
2 CONC etruce with the Scots and Warden of the Scottish Marches (the las t oft
2 CONC hese till Whitsun that year only) Feb 1326/7, being one of only f ourEn
2 CONC glish nobles not to be deprived of their Scottish possessions und er th
2 CONC epeace terms; granted by Edward III Warkworth Castle 1328, Keepe r Bamb
2 CONC urghCastle April 1330, overseer of array (local defence) for nor thernc
2 CONC ounties July 1330, envoy to negotiate peace with the French Ja n 1330/1
2 CONC ,Justiciar of Eastern March Feb 1330/1, Warden of the March 13 32, pres
2 CONC entat Siege of Berwick (of which subsequently Keeper) and Edwa rd III's
2 CONC victory over Scots at Halidon Hill July 1333, chief commission er to Sc
2 CONC otsParliament  to ensure Edward Balliol honoured his pledge t o do homa
2 CONC ge toEdward III and cede southwest Scotland Oct 1333, membe r of counci
2 CONC l ofregency during Edward III's absence overseas 1339 and 1 340, comman
2 CONC ded 3rddivision of English victory of Neville's Cross ove r the Scots 1
2 CONC 346,following which David II of Scotland was imprisoned i n Bamburgh Ca
2 CONC stle,commissioner to negotiate final peace with Scots 135 0; married Id
2 CONC oine orIdonea de Clifford (died 24 Aug 1365), daughter o f 1st Lord (Ba
2 CONC ron)Clifford, and died late Feb 1351/2.  [Burke's Peerag e]
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry de Percy, 2nd Lord Percy, of Alnwick, had a grant from the crow n i
2 CONC nthe 2nd Edward III of the reversion of the barony and castle ofWar kwo
2 CONC rth, &c. He had summons to parliament from 1322 tothe time of hisde ath
2 CONC , 26 February, 1351-2, when he was s. by his eldest son (by Idonia, dau
2 CONC . of Robert, Lord Clifford), Henry de Percy, 3rd Lord Percy, ofAlnw ick
2 CONC . [Sir Bernard Burke, Dormant, Abeyant, Forfeited, and ExtinctPeera ges
2 CONC , Burke's Peerage, Ltd., London, 1883, p. 423, Percy, BaronsPercy , Ear
2 CONC ls of Northumberland, &c.]
