1 NOTE  http://worldconnect.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi&#00063;op=GET&db=roya l
2 CONC ancestors&id=I8357
2 CONT
2 CONT Poet Robert Frost is a descendant
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert I, by name ROBERT The MAGNIFICENT, or The DEVIL, French ROBER T l
2 CONC eMAGNIFIQUE, or le DIABLE (d. July 1035, Nicaea), duke of Normandy( 102
2 CONC 7-35), the younger son of Richard II of Normandy and the father, by his m
2 CONC istress Arlette, of William the Conqueror of England. On the deat h of h
2 CONC is father (1026/27), Robert contested the duchy with his elder b rother R
2 CONC ichard III, legally the heir, until the latter's opportune dea th a few y
2 CONC ears later. A strong ruler, Robert succeeded in exacting th e obedience o
2 CONC f his vassals. On the death of Robert II the Pious, kin g of France (10
2 CONC 31),a crisis arose over the succession to the French th rone. The Duke g
2 CONC ave hissupport to Henry I against the party favourin g his younger brot
2 CONC her; in reward for his services he demanded and rece ived the Vexin Fra
2 CONC nçais, a territory not far north of Paris. A patro n of the monastic re
2 CONC form movement, he died while returning from a pilg rimage to Jerusalem.
2 CONC [Encyclopaedia Britannica CD '97]
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert contributed to the restoration of Henry King of France to his t h
2 CONC rone, and received from the gratitude of that monarch, the Vexin, a s a
2 CONC n additional to his patrimonial domains. In the 8th year of his rei gn, c
2 CONC uriosity or devotion induced him to undertake a pilgrimage to th e Holy L
2 CONC and, where the fatiges of the journey and the heat of the clim ate so i
2 CONC mpaired his consitution he died on his way home.
