1 NOTE  Isabella plotted the death of Edward, and had him murdered on Septembe r 2
2 CONC 1, 1327 at Berkeley Castle, Gloucester, by having a red-hot spit th rus
2 CONC t through his bowels.
2 CONT Roger Mortimer was the 1st Earl of March.  He opposed Edward II and th e D
2 CONC espencers in the wars of 1321-22.  He escaped to France where Quee n Is
2 CONC abella, Edward's official Queen Consort, became his mistress. The y  in
2 CONC vaded England and forced Edward II to abdicate January 25, 1327 , in fa
2 CONC vour of Edward's son, Edward III.   Isabella and Mortimer share d the  R
2 CONC egency until they were overthrown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger Mortimer and his gang were overthrown in 1330 by Edward III, an d M
2 CONC ortimer himself was executed.  Isabella was forced into "honorabl e ret
2 CONC irement"  from public life; she died August 22, 1358.  Her tomb w as lo
2 CONC st during the Reformation.
2 CONT
2 CONT - Alison Weir, BRITAIN'S ROYAL FAMILIES
2 CONT
