2 CONT EARLDOM of CORNWALL (I) 1141 to 1175
2 CONT
2 CONT Reynold de Dunstanville, one of the 14 illegitimate children of Henr y I
2 CONC ,was the son of Sybil, daughter of Sir Robert Corbet, of Alcester , co.
2 CONC Warwick, and having m. &#00063;Mabel, daughter and (in her issue ) heir o
2 CONC f William Fitz Richard, a man of huge estates in Cornwall, wa s created a
2 CONC bout Apr 1141, Earl of Cornwall, probably by the Empress Ma ud, but the t
2 CONC itle was fully recognised subsequently by King Stephen .  He was a witn
2 CONC ess to the compromise between Stephen and Henry, 1153 .  Sheriff of Dev
2 CONC on, 1173-75.  He was in command, ex parte Regis, Oc t 1173, against the r
2 CONC ebellious Barons.  He d. spm legit, at Chertsey , Surrey, 1 July 1175,a
2 CONC nd was buried in the Abbey of Reading, when th e Earldom reverted to th
2 CONC e Crown.  [Complete Peerage, III:429 as correc ted by XIV:207]
