2 CONC dation of the Holy Roma n Empire.Though Charlemagne did not use the tit
2 CONC le, he is considered th efirst Holy Roman emperor (see Holy Roman Empir
2 CONC e).Reform and Renaissan ceCharlemagne had deep sympathy for the peasant
2 CONC s and believed thatgove rnment should be for the benefit of the governe
2 CONC d. When hecame to the t hrone, various local governors, called "counts,
2 CONC "had become lax and opp ressive. To reform them, he expanded thework of i
2 CONC nvestigators, calle d missi dominici. He prescribedtheir duties in docu
