2 CONC nd a noble. The y rode to all partsof the realm, inspecting government, a
2 CONC dministerin g justice, and reawakening all citizens to their civil andr
2 CONC eligious du ties.Twice a year Charlemagne summoned the chief men of the e
2 CONC mpire tod iscuss its affairs. In all problems he was the final arbiter,
2 CONC even in c hurch issues, and he largely unified church and state.Charlem
2 CONC agne wa s a tireless reformer who tried to improve hispeople's lot in m
2 CONC any way s. He set up money standards toencourage commerce, tried to bui
2 CONC ld a Rh ine-Danube canal, andurged better farming methods. He especiall
2 CONC y worke d to spreadeducation and Christianity in every class of people.
