1 NOTE  Adding Grandy line I found all this connection and very hard to add du e t
2 CONC o spellings and dates but I think its correct by my "Creedo Logic " !!
2 CONT
2 CONT http://worldconnect.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi&#00063;op=GET&db=jlan g
2 CONC maid&id=I4175 < Got notes from this site.
2 CONT
2 CONT John was Earl of Lancaster, Richmond, Derby and Lincoln, Duke of Aquit a
2 CONC ine and Lord of Beaufort and Nogent, King of Castile and Leon (whil e m
2 CONC arried to Constanza). As Earl of Lancaster, John of Gaunt (Ghent) w as t
2 CONC he head of the house of Lancaster. His son by his first wife (hi s 4th c
2 CONC ousin Blanche Plantagenet) became Henry IV the first King of th e house o
2 CONC f Lancaster. Blanche's father, Henry Plantagenet, was the fir st Duke o
2 CONC f Lancaster and a descendant of Hamelin Plantagenet, 1st Ear l of Lanca
2 CONC ster, and half-brother of Henry II.John had a lifelong attra ction to h
2 CONC is cousin, Catherine of Roet, his mother's niece, grand daug hter of Gu
2 CONC illaume IV, Count of Hainault. Catherine was first the gover ness of hi
2 CONC s and Blanch's children while she was married to Sir Hugh d e Swynford. S
2 CONC he became his mistress about 1373 shortly after he marrie d Constanza. W
2 CONC hen Constanza became aware of this she went home to dadd y, taking her d
2 CONC aughter with her and John moved Catherine to Beaufort C astle in Anjou, F
2 CONC rance (the source of the surname given to their child ren). This incest
2 CONC uous relationship continued even after Constanza died . He married Cath
2 CONC erine after Constanza's death, and the Pope legitimiz ed their four chi
2 CONC ldren (all born before Constanza died). Catherine's s ister, Philippa, m
2 CONC arried Geoffrey Chaucer, author of the Canterbury Ta les.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: John of Gaunt had a tempestuous romance with Katherine Roet whil e h
2 CONC e was married to Constanza of Castile. For much of the time Katheri ne s
2 CONC tayed at Beaufort Castle in Anjou and hence her children were name d Be
2 CONC aufort. After Constanza died, John married Katherine at Lincoln Ca thed
2 CONC ral and formally adopted her children (the youngest, Joan Beaufor t was a
2 CONC bout 16 when the marriage took place).
