2 CONT Sir Hugh le Despenser, 1st Lord (Baron) Despenser of the putative 126 4 c
2 CONC reation; knighted c1244, Constable of Horston Castle 1255, one of t wel
2 CONC ve representatives by the barons at the Parliament (a convention ra the
2 CONC r than full Parliament as recognised today) of Oxford June 1258 t o pre
2 CONC ss for action by Henry III to right the wrongs done them and nego tiate w
2 CONC ith the King's Council, nominated Justiciar of England by the b arons a
2 CONC nd accordingly appointed to that post by Henry 1260 but dismiss ed by h
2 CONC im 1261, renominated 1263 by the barons and reappointed with He nry's a
2 CONC greement, Constable of the Tower of London 1263 and Devizes, Ox ford, O
2 CONC rford, and Nottingham Castles 1264; called to a form of Parliam ent 24 D
2 CONC ec 1264 by writ whereby according to peerage law doctrine as i t stood a
2 CONC t the time of the judgement of 1604 he may be reckoned to hav e been cr
2 CONC eated Lord le Despenser; and was killed at the Battle of Eves ham 4 Aug 1
2 CONC 265, fighting for Simon de Montfort, Earl of Leicester, aga inst Henry I
2 CONC II. [Burke's Peerage]
