1 NOTE  !See notes of husb.
2 CONT Summary (revised Aug 1999):  Ord work done by name of Mrs. Catherine
2 CONT or Katherine Winslow, spouse of Kenelm.  His will named his wife
2 CONT Katherine but it is not clear whether she is the mother of his childre n
2 CONC .
2 CONT A manuscript in the Family History Library in Salt Lake City (on
2 CONT microfiche 6019063) says Katherine was probably "his last wife".  A
2 CONT series of articles by John G. Hunt in "The American Genealogist" vol
2 CONT 41-43 and in "New Eng. Hist. and Gen. Reg." vol 121-124 describes his
2 CONT research concerning the first wife.  The most promising theory is
2 CONT Elizabeth, daughter of John Foliott, but it is not conclusive.
2 CONT An article by Mahomet G. Jones, Ogden, Utah, found in pamphlet form in
2 CONT the Family History Library in Salt Lake City, reviews the various
2 CONT theories and comes to the conclusion that none of the conjectures abou t
2 CONT the wife of Kenelm Winslow of Droitwich are probable enough to accept.
2 CONT
