2 CONT ENCYCLOPÆDIA BRITANNICA , 1960, Vol 6, page 605: Reynold's son, Robert , m
2 CONC arried Mary, daughger of William De Vernon, earl of Devon and of th e I
2 CONC sle of Wright.  He was succeed in 1242 by his son, John...
2 CONT -----------------------------------
2 CONT Robert de Courtenay; feudal Lord of Okehampton and Sutton Courtenay; S h
2 CONC eriff of Devon and Oxon, Castellan of Exeter and Oxford, inherited 3 1 J
2 CONC uly 1219 from his mother the great Honour of Okehampton in Devon, a mou
2 CONC nting to 92 knights' fees; King John granted him the right to coi n tin i
2 CONC n Devon and Cornwall in 1215. [Burke's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT While Ancestral Roots names Robert a Baron of Okehampton, Burke's Peer a
2 CONC ge states that he was a feudal Lord of Okehampton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maloney, Hendrick &amp; Others - J. H. Maloney
