2 CONT
2 CONT Renaud de Courtenay; Sheriff of Devon and Castellan of Exeter; marrie d b
2 CONC y 1178 Hawise, feudal Lady of Okehampton, daughter and coheir of Wi lli
2 CONC am de Crucy (or Geoffrey de Crunes (Craon)) by his wife Maud d'Avra nch
2 CONC es, the latter being heiress of Baldwin Fitz Gilbert's family, whic h h
2 CONC ad held the honour of Okehampton and the Shrievalty of Devon 1080-1 142
2 CONC . [Burke's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Reginald de Courtenay, son by (1st wife, an unidentifed woman whom I h a
2 CONC ve unsourced as Hawise Deincourt), b. c 1150, d. 27 Sep 1194, burie d F
2 CONC ord Abbey, co. Devon; held barony of Oakhampton (in right of wife) ; m. H
2 CONC awise de Courcy, d. 31 July 1219, lady of Oakhampton, half-siste r of h
2 CONC is father's second wife [Maud, daughter of Robert Fitz Edith (il legiti
2 CONC mate son of King Henry I of England, by Edith, daughter of Forn) , by M
2 CONC aud (d'Avranches) de Courcy, widow of William de Courcy], daught er and h
2 CONC eir of William de Courcy, by wife, Maud d'Avranches, lady of O akhampto
2 CONC n, and of du Sap in Normandy, daughter and heir of Robert d'Av ranches, l
2 CONC ord of Oakhampton, co. Devon. [Ancestral Roots]
2 CONT
2 CONT Maloney, Hendrick &amp; Others - J. H. Maloney
