2 CONC s claims were powerfully upheld in England by her h alf brother Robert o
2 CONC f Gloucester and her uncle King David I of Scotlan d. Matilda and Rober
2 CONC t landed at Arundel in September 1139, and she wa s for a short while b
2 CONC esieged in the castle. But Stephen soon allowed h er to join her brothe
2 CONC r, who had gone to the west country, where she ha d much support; after a s
2 CONC tay at Bristol, she settled at Gloucester.Sh e came nearest to success i
2 CONC n the summer of 1141, after Stephen had bee n captured at Lincoln in Fe
