2 CONC ter in April, she entered London in Jun e; but her arrogance and tactle
2 CONC ss demands for money provoked the citiz ens to chase her away to Oxford b
2 CONC efore she could be crowned queen. He r forces were routed at Winchester i
2 CONC n September 1141, and thereafter s he maintained a steadily weakening r
2 CONC esistance in the west country. He r well-known escape from Oxford Castl
2 CONC e over the frozen River Thames to ok place in December 1142.Normandie h
