1 NOTE  EARLDOM of ORKNEY [NOR] - subject to King of Norway until after 1379
2 CONT
2 CONT RAGNVALD I the Wise, called the Morejarl, son of Eystein Glumra, Jar l o
2 CONC f the Uplanders in Norway, grandson of Ivar son of Halfdan the Old , wa
2 CONC s made Jarl of North and South More and of Raumsdal in Norway by K ing H
2 CONC arald Haarfagri after his victory of Solskiel circa 869 over Hunt hiof, K
2 CONC ing of More, and Nokve, King of Raumsdal. In that year he surpr ised Ve
2 CONC rmund, King of Fiordeland, at Notsdal and burned him in his hal l with 9
2 CONC 0 men. Later King Harald married his sister Swanhilda and ha d issue, I
2 CONC n (&#00063;) 874 King Harald made an expedition to the Nordr eys (Orkne
2 CONC y and Shetland) to enforce his authority over those who ha d fled thith
2 CONC er in order to escape from it in Norway. Either during thi s expedition o
2 CONC r previously at the battle of Hafrsfiord circa 872 Ivar , the eldest so
2 CONC n of Ragnvald, was killed and the King gave the Orkney s and Shetlands t
2 CONC o Ragnvald as compensation. When the King started hom e for Norway, (&#
2 CONC 00063;) Spring 875, Ragnvald, who went with him, gav e the islands to h
2 CONC is brother Sigurd, and the King confirmed the transf er, Ragnvald was s
2 CONC urprised in his hall and burned alive circa 894 by H alfdan Haaleg and G
2 CONC udred Liomi, King Harald's sons by Snaefrid, dau. o f Swasi.
2 CONT
2 CONT By his wife Ragnhild, dau. of Hrolf Nefia, he had 3 sons: Ivar, who wa s k
2 CONC illed in battle ut supra, Rolf the Ganger, afterwards 1st Duke of N orm
2 CONC andy, and Thori the Silent, who was made Jarl of More in successio n to h
2 CONC is father by King Harald Haarfagri circa 894, after Gudred Liomi , who h
2 CONC ad seized More on the death of Jarl Ragnvald, had been disposse ssed by t
2 CONC he King. By an earlier union with a nameless girl, whose kind red were a
2 CONC ll slave-born, Ragnvald had 3 sons, described as bastards: H allad, 4th E
2 CONC arl of Orkney, Turf-Einar, 5th Earl of Orkney, and Hrollau g, an unwarl
2 CONC ike man, who settled at Eyiafiord in Iceland and had issue . [Complete P
2 CONC eerage, X:Appendix A:3-4]
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Rogenwald was a supporter of King Harold Harfagr, and assisted him i n o
2 CONC btaining the mastery over the other independent Norwegian chiefs, a nd i
2 CONC n establishing himself as King of all Norway. He was Earl of Mor e and R
2 CONC aumdahl in Norway, and in 888, he obtained from King Harold a g rant of t
2 CONC he Orkney and Shetland islands. One of his sons, Rollo, conqu ered Neus
2 CONC tria, founded the line of sovereign Dukes of Normandy, and wa s ancesto
2 CONC r to William the Conqueror. [Sir Bernard Burke, Dormant, Abey ant, Forf
2 CONC eited, and Extinct Peerages, Burke's Peerage, Ltd., London, 1 883, p. 4
2 CONC 92, Sinclair, Earl of Orkney]
