2 CONT Henry de Percy, 1st Lord (Baron) Percy, so created by writ of summon s t
2 CONC oParliament 6 Feb 1298/9; born posthumously c25 March 1273; serve d inE
2 CONC dward I's Welsh campaign 1294, knighter 1296, fought at Battle o f Dunb
2 CONC ar27 April 1296, in which his maternal grandfather the 7th Ear l of Sur
2 CONC reybeat off an attack by the Scots, Warden of Galloway and Ayr shire Se
2 CONC p1296, Justiciar of Dumfries 1297, Jt Justiciar of Cumberland , Lancs a
2 CONC ndWestmorland 1297, Member of Council of Regency, during Edwa rd I's ab
2 CONC senceoverseas 1297-98, fought at English victory of Falkirk o ver the S
2 CONC cots1298, at Siege of Carlaverock 1300; accompanied Edwar d I at Siege o
2 CONC fStirling 1304, King's Lt and Captain over all men-at-ar ms of the West
2 CONC Borders 1306, Constable of Scarborough Castle March 1307 /8; bought 19 N
2 CONC ov1309 from Anthony Beck or Bek, Bishop of Durham, th e Barony (here at
2 CONC erritorial entity carrying certain feudal rights, rat her than a title o
2 CONC fhonour in the modern sense) of Alnwick, Co Northumb erland, thus found
2 CONC ingthe Percy ascendancy there (for the bulk of the l ands previouslybel
2 CONC onging to the family had been further south in Yorks hire, Sussex, orHa
2 CONC nts); one of the magnates opposed to Edward II, too k part in theappoin
2 CONC tment of the Lords Ordainers, an executive committe e entrusted withgiv
2 CONC ing specific expression to that opposition; Keepe r of the Bishopric of
2 CONC Durham pro tem March 1311, Justice of the Fores t beyond Trent and Keep
2 CONC erof Bamburgh Castle Dec 1311, Jt Keeper of th e Marches c1311; married
2 CONC &#00063; byJune 1294 Eleanor (died July or Au g 1328), sister of Richar
2 CONC d de Arundel,and died between 2 and 10 Oct 13 14.  [Burke's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry de Percy, 9th feudal lord, was summoned to parliament from 6Febr u
2 CONC ary, 1299 (27th Edward I) to 29 July, 1315 (8th Edward II). Thisnoble m
2 CONC an obtained, 19 November, 1309, from Anthony Beck, bishop ofDurham, b y p
2 CONC urchase, a grant of the Barony of Alnwick, co.Northumberland. His l ord
2 CONC ship was one of the great barons who subscribed,in 1301, the celebr ate
2 CONC d letter to Pope Boniface VIII, upon the attempt ofhis holiness t o int
2 CONC erpose in the affairs of the kingdom, intimating,"That their kin g was n
2 CONC ot to answer in judgment, for any rights of thecrown of England , befor
2 CONC e any tribunal under heaven, &c., and that, by thehelp of God , they wo
2 CONC uld resolutely, and with all their force, maintainagainst al l men." He m
2 CONC . Eleanor, dau. of John FitzAlan, Earl of Arundel,d. in 13 15, and was s
2 CONC . by his eldest son, Henry de Percy, 2nd Lord Percy.[Si r Bernard Burke
2 CONC , Dormant, Abeyant, Forfeited, and Extinct Peerages,Bur ke's Peerage, L
2 CONC td., London, 1883, p. 423, Percy, Barons Percy, Earlso f Northumberland
2 CONC , &c.]
2 CONT
