1 NOTE  King Robert Capet II of /France/
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of King Hugh Capet and King of France from 996-1031. Robert was ca l
2 CONC led "the Pious" because of his humility and charity.
2 CONT
2 CONT !Our Noble & Gentle Families of Royal Descent Together with Their Pate r
2 CONC nal
2 CONT Ancestry by Joseph Foster p 178 1884 Edition:
2 CONT
2 CONT !Ridipath's Histories; Burk's Landed Gentry; Gareth Rice;
2 CONT
2 CONT !Royal Ancestors of Some American Families by Michel Call SLC 1989#425
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert II., the Pious, King of France from 996 to 1031, was born in Or l
2 CONC eansin 971, died in Melun in 1031, buried at St. Denis, reigned fro m 9
2 CONC 96 to July 20, 1031. He was a royal composer,chorister, and poet, w ho m
2 CONC ight have ruled Italy but preferred that his palace should be hi s cloi
2 CONC ster, where he lived in the enjoyment of melody and song. He con ducted t
2 CONC he matins and vespers in his royal robes. He was a very devou t man. He m
2 CONC arried in 988(1) Rosala (Rozela), daughter of King Berenga r II. of Ita
2 CONC ly, but this marriage was repudiated in 992, married in 99 7 (2) Bertha o
2 CONC f Bourgogne, daughter of Conrad of Burgundy, who died af ter 1017, also d
2 CONC ivorced in 1003/5; and (3) Constance Berengar (Berenge r) of Artes, bor
2 CONC n circa 987, died in Melunin 1032 buired at St. Denis , daughter of Wil
2 CONC liam Berengar II (Berenger), Count of Provence,
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard 111, Duke of Normandy who dsp the uncle of William the Conquer o
2 CONC r who married Baldwin V. de I'Isle count of flanders and of Artois.
2 CONT
