2 CONT
2 CONT King of France (987-96), the first of the Capetians. He was the son o f H
2 CONC ugh the Great, to whose vast territories he succeeded in 956. Afte r th
2 CONC e death of Louis V, last Carolingian King of France, the nobles an d pr
2 CONC elate selected him king in 987, setting aside the last Carolingia n cla
2 CONC imant, Charles I of Lower Lorraine. In order to secure the succes sion, H
2 CONC ugh took as his associate his son Robert (later King Robert II) ; he ga
2 CONC ve away much of his land to secure the dynasty.
2 CONT He spent much of his reign fighting Charles, and later became involve d i
2 CONC na controversy with the papacy over the deposition (and death) of t he C
2 CONC arolingian Archbishop of Reims.
2 CONT -- The Columbia Encyclopedia
