2 CONT !UPDATE: 7 AUG 1993
2 CONT Sources: RC 235, 250; Coe; A. Roots; AF; K and Q of Britain; Alfred th e G
2 CONC reat by P.H. Helm; Smallwood.
2 CONT Princess of France. Queen of Wessex and England. Baldwin was her secon d h
2 CONC usband.
2 CONT Helm: Judith, daughter of Charles the Bald; married Ethelwulf 1 Oct. 8 5
2 CONC 6 when she was about 12 years old. Married (2) in 858 Ethelbald, so n o
2 CONC f Ethelwulf. Ethelbald died in 860 and Judith was "packed off bac k to F
2 CONC rance." "There she was visited by Baldwin the "Iron-Arm", late r count o
2 CONC f Flanders, and helped by her brother, Judith eloped with Bal dwin and f
2 CONC led to Rome. Her furious father persuaded the French bishop s to excomm
2 CONC nicate her lover, but the Pope, Nicholas I, was more sympat hetic. In t
2 CONC he end the king gave way--but he refused to attend the wedd ing! Thirty y
2 CONC ears later one of Alfred's daughters, Aelfthryth, marrie d the son of J
2 CONC udith and Baldwin."
