1 NOTE  Though peerage articles, including CP [Complete Peerage] V 472, have l o
2 CONC ng identified Ida No. 27 [ie. this Ida] as a daughter of Gen. 26 [Wil l
2 CONC iam Longspee & Ela FitzPatrick], it is clear that their daughter Id a a
2 CONC ctually married (1) Ralph de Somery (dsp) and (2) bef. 1220 Willia m Be
2 CONC auchamp, of Bedford (see 122A-29 (CP XII (1) note g, which says th is I
2 CONC da living 10 Apr 1262).  Moriarty (ms. at NEHGS) suggested Willia m Lon
2 CONC gespee had two daughters Ida, or Idoine, which may be correct.  B ut th
2 CONC ere appears almost a generation difference between the two Ida's , so t
2 CONC he chronicler may have missed a generation and Ida No 27 may b e the da
2 CONC ughter of William's son William II (122-29).  [Ancestral Roots ]
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: based on the above, I am making Ida, a daughter of William II Lo n
2 CONC gespee.
