1 NOTE  Sir Thomas de Furnivall(e), 1st Lord (Baron) Furinvall(e), so create d b
2 CONC y writ of summons to Parliament 24 June 1295; fought at Battle of F alk
2 CONC irk against the Scots 1298; married 1st by Jan 1272/3 Joan, daughte r o
2 CONC f 1st Lord (Baron) le Despenser of the putative 1264 creation, an d had [
2 CONC Thomas, Catherine, Eleanor].  The 1st Lord (Baron) Furnivall(e ) marrie
2 CONC d 2nd by 8 June 1322 Elizabeth (died Aug 1354), widow of 2nd L ord (Bar
2 CONC on) Montagu of the 1299 creation and daughter of Sir Piers d e Mo(u)ntf
2 CONC ort, of Beaudesert, Warwicks, and died just prior to 18 Apri l 1332, ha
2 CONC ving had another son William, whether by his 1st or 2nd wif e is unknow
2 CONC n.  [Burke's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------- -
2 CONC ---  ---------------------------------------------------
2 CONT Following copied from Susan Cary, World Connect db=poliksa, rootsweb.c o
2 CONC m:
