2 CONC ---  ---------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas de Furnival, 1st Baron Furnival, who had a summons, in the 22n d o
2 CONC f Edward I, amongst other great men, to attend the King in order t o ad
2 CONC vise of the affairs of the realm, and having done so, received com mand t
2 CONC o repair to Portsmouth, upon the first of the ensuing September , well f
2 CONC itted with horse and arms, for the expedition then intended ag ainst Fr
2 CONC ance. In the next year, 23 June, 1295, he was first summoned t o Parlia
2 CONC ment as a baron, and from that period his lordship appears, fo r severa
2 CONC l years, to have taken a distinguished part in the Scottish wa rs. In 2
2 CONC 7th of Edward I he was constituted Captain-General and Lieuten ant to t
2 CONC he King, for the Counties of Nottingham and Derby, and had sum mons to P
2 CONC arliament uninterruptedly until 27 January, 1332, 3rd of Edwa rd III, b
2 CONC ut he did not hold lands by barony. Lord Furnival married Eli zabeth, d
2 CONC aughter of Peter de Montfort, Jr., of Beldesert Castle, Count y Warwick
2 CONC , and was succeeded at his decease by his eldest son, Thomas.
