1 SEX M
1 _UID A2BAB9CE5CF24A86AE26CBA98CEAC26DEE52
1 _AMTID 162143285629:1030:164657654
1 CHAN
2 DATE 2 NOV 2019
1 NOTE  Roger de Mohaut, 2nd son of Eustace de Arden, Baron of Hawarden, hered i
2 CONC tary seneschal of Cheshire.  [Magna Charta Sureties]
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------- -
2 CONC --- ----
2 CONT I find a number of references to the husband of Cicely d'Aubigny as Ay l
2 CONC mer de Montalt.  Whether Aylmer is an elder brother of Roger with a m i
2 CONC xup as to the wife, or whether Aylmer is another name for Roger and t h
2 CONC e elder brother died young, I do not know.  The excerpt below is obvi o
2 CONC usly somewhat inaccurate describing a man of age in 1174 who died i n 1
2 CONC 260 (the death date matches Roger's, as well as the estate in Risin g N
2 CONC orfolk).  I copied the information from Susan Cary, World Connect d b=p
2 CONC oliksa, rootsweb.com:
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------- -
2 CONC --- -----
2 CONT
2 CONT Aylmer (or Andomar) founded the Yorkshire and only surviving branch o f t
2 CONC he family. In 1174, accompanying the expedition against William th e Li
2 CONC on, Andomar had the good fortune to make the Scottish monarch pris oner
2 CONC , by surprise; and conveying the royal captive to Henry II. He wa s dee
2 CONC med one of the most potent feudal lords in the time of Henry III . and a
2 CONC ccompanied Prince Edward to the Holy Land. Being constantly emp loyed a
2 CONC gainst the Welsh, his lands at Montalt were wrested from him b y David, P
2 CONC rince of Wales, but restored in 1240. He m. Cecilia, secon d sister and o
2 CONC ne of the co-heirs of Hugh de Albini, Earl of Arundel, b y whom he acqu
2 CONC ired the manor of Castle Rising, in Norfolk, with othe r extensive esta
2 CONC tes. To equip himself for Palestine this great baron c onveyed, for a s
2 CONC um of money, a large portion of the woods and revenue s which he posses
2 CONC sed at Coventry, in right of Cecilia, his wife, to th e monks of that p
2 CONC lace. He died in 1260, and was s. by his elder son, J ohn the 4th Baron b
2 CONC y tenure.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Based on the Yorkshire reference in the preceding and the inheritanc e o
2 CONC f Bingley, West Ride Yorkshire by Roger's granddaughter Ellen, I a m pr
2 CONC esuming that Roger held Bingley at one time.
2 CONT
2 CONT Click here for <a href="http://www.dersingham.com/Attractions.htm">Pho t
2 CONC o of Castle Rising</a> (use browser back arrow to return)
2 CONT
2 CONT Click here for <a href="http://www.castlewales.com/hawrdn.html">Phot o o
2 CONC f Hawarden/Montalt Castle</a> (use browser back arrow to return)
2 CONT
