1 NOTE  Sir John de Grey, of Rotherfield, d. 17 Oct 1311, MP 1297.  [Magna Cha r
2 CONC ta Sureties]
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT SIR JOHN DE GREY, son and heir, was summoned 26 January 1296/7 to a Co u
2 CONC ncil, and was summoned for Military Service from 30 March 1298 to 2 7 S
2 CONC eptember 1299 (k). He was an executor of Edmund, Earl of Cornwall ; was p
2 CONC resent at the Siege of Carlaverock. He married Margaret, 4th an d young
2 CONC est daughter of William DE ODDINGESELES by Ela, daughter of Wal ter Fit
2 CONC zRobert, of Woodham Walter, Essex, and sister and coh. of Edmun d DE OD
2 CONC DINGESELES, of Solihull and Maxstokc, co. Warwick. He died 17 O ctober 1
2 CONC 311. His widow had assignment of dower 20 January 1311/2, an d licence t
2 CONC o marry whom she would 10 June 1312. She appears to have ma rried, 2ndl
2 CONC y, in or before 1319, Robert DE MOREBY, of Moreby, co. York .  [Complet
2 CONC e Peerage VI:145, (transcribed by Dave Utzinger)]
2 CONT
2 CONT (k) Subsequent writs addressed during his lifetime to John de Grey ref e
2 CONC r to John de Grey of Wilton.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT John de Grey, then twenty-four years of age, who, soon after doing hi s h
2 CONC omage, had livery of his inheritance, and in the 25th Edward I [129 7], h
2 CONC ad summons to the parliament then held at Westminster, as a baron . Thi
2 CONC s nobleman appears to have taken part in the Scottish wars of Edw ard I
2 CONC . His lordship m. Margaret, dau. and co-heiress of William de Odi ngsel
2 CONC ls, of Maxtock, co. Warwick, and dying 5th Edward II [1312], wa s s. by h
2 CONC is son, John de Grey, 2nd baron. [Sir Bernard Burke, Dormant , Abeyant, F
2 CONC orfeited and Extinct Peerages, Burke's Peerage, Ltd., Lond on, England, 1
2 CONC 883, p. 247, Grey, Barons Grey, of Rotherfield, co. Oxfo rd]
