2 CONT
2 CONT It is uncertain whether Eleanor was the only child born to Miolicent s m
2 CONC arriage to John de Mohaut, or if she was the first child born to he r s
2 CONC econd marriage to Eudo la Zouche.  Jim Weber's note appears convinc ing t
2 CONC hat she was born to the first marriage:
2 CONT Jim Weber Note:  While MCS names her straight out as "Ellen la Zouche " a
2 CONC nd doesn't even mention John de Mohaut as 1st husband of her mother , A
2 CONC ncestral Roots (in line 38, which is the la Zouche line) lists he r as t
2 CONC he next generation after Eudo la Zouche (implying that Eudo wa s the fa
2 CONC ther, while noting that Milicent de Cantelou had married Joh n de Mohau
2 CONC t first), but just names her "Eleanor or Ellen" without a su rname (Whi
2 CONC le they almost always give a surname! Is AR hedging its bets &#00063;). A
2 CONC R gives as supporting evidence the following: "(Feudal Aid s 6:21,23 re
2 CONC fers to 'Elienora de Zuche' as holding the manor of Bingle y of her mot
2 CONC her 'Milisenta de Monte Alto' in 1284-5; Rev. C Moor, Knig hts of Edwar
2 CONC d I 2:183-184)." That quote leads me to think that Ellen w as a daughte
2 CONC r of Milicent and John de Monte Alto / Mohaut / Montalt /M ontault and w
2 CONC as "adopted" by 2nd husband Eudo la Zouche. Her mother Mi licent held t
2 CONC he manor of Bingley in the name of Monte Alto for her dau ghter by her f
2 CONC irst marriage.
2 CONT Certainly if Ellen held Bingley in 1284-5, she might have been of ag e (
2 CONC her mother did not die until 1298/99), which means she could have b een b
2 CONC orn as early as 1263, which would certainly make her a child of J ohn & M
2 CONC ilicent.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maloney, Hendrick &amp; Others - J. H. Maloney
