1 NOTE  BARONY OF MARMION (II)
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN MARMION, LORD MARMION, son and heir, was born circa 1292. In Octo b
2 CONC er 1313 the name of John Marmyon the younger occurs among those of th e a
2 CONC dherents of Thomas, Earl of Lancaster, who were pardoned for the de ath o
2 CONC f Piers de Gavaston. As John Marmion le fiz he was summoned for m ilita
2 CONC ry service against the Scots in 1314, and again, as John Marmion , in 1
2 CONC 322 and 1323. In August 1322 he had protection for going with th e Earl o
2 CONC f Richmond to Scotland; and in October he was appointed a comm issioner o
2 CONC f array for the North Riding. In February 1324/5 he was summ oned to pa
2 CONC ss into Guienne under the command of the Earl Warenne. He wa s summoned t
2 CONC o Parliament 3 December 1326, by writ directed Johanni Mar myoun. In Se
2 CONC ptember 1327 he was named on a commission of oyer and term iner for Yor
2 CONC kshire; and in the same year, with Maud his wife, he mad e a settlement i
2 CONC n special tail male of the manors of Tanfield and Cart horpe. In May 13
2 CONC 29 he had a protection for three years on going on pil grimage to the H
2 CONC oly Land. In October 1331 he complained that while h e was under the Ki
2 CONC ng's protection certain persons broke his park at Ta nfield, hunted the
2 CONC re and carried away his deer. In July 1332 he was or dered to choose 20 a
2 CONC rchers for the King's expedition to Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Maud, who is said to have been a daughter of Thomas, LORD F U
2 CONC RNIVALLE (j). He is said to have died 30 April 1335.  [Complete Peera g
2 CONC e VIII:520-1, (transcribed by Dave Utzinger)]
2 CONT
2 CONT (j) In 1343 as widow of John Marmyoun, chivaler, she caused a settleme n
2 CONC t to be made of the manors of West Tanfield, East Tanfield, Carthorpe , M
2 CONC anfield, and Brough, and other specified property, including the ad vow
2 CONC sons of West Tanfield and Wath, of the hospital of St. Giles by Bro mpt
2 CONC on Bridge, and the chantries of West Tanfield, Little Langton, an d Wat
2 CONC h; to hold to Maud and the heirs male of her body; remainder to J ohn d
2 CONC e Grey of Rotherfield and Avice his wife and to John Maryon son o f the s
2 CONC aid John and Alice, and the heirs of the bodies of the said Joh n de Gr
2 CONC ey and Avice; remainder to the heirs of Avice's body; remainde r to Joh
2 CONC n Bernak and Joan his wife, and the heirs of Joan's body; rema inder to A
2 CONC vice's right heirs.  In 1346 she is described as 'Domina d e Marmion'; a
2 CONC nd in 1348 she had licence to crenellate the manor of Wes t Tanfield. H
2 CONC er name was commemorated in "the three chauntereys calle d Mawde Marmeo
2 CONC n in the parysshe church of Tanfield".  On 20 Feb 1361/ 2 John of Gaunt g
2 CONC ranted a licence in mortmain for the grant of land i n the manors of We
2 CONC st Tanfield and Carthorpe to certain chaplains to ce lebrate in the chu
2 CONC rch of West Tanfield for the good of his soul and th e souls of John Ma
2 CONC rmyon and Maude his wife.
