2 DATE 2 NOV 2019
1 NOTE  AKA ->> Herbastus De Crepon
2 CONT http://worldconnect.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi&#00063;op=GET&db=pusc h
2 CONC &id=I044238
2 CONT
2 CONT RC 166 says Gunnor's father was Herbastus De Crepon, Forester of Arque s (
2 CONC in Denmark). Were there two foresters, the father of Gunnor and Sai nfr
2 CONC ida and also the husband of Sainfrida&#00063; Or did the story beco me t
2 CONC angled over the years&#00063;
2 CONT
2 CONT I had quite a work to clean up connect & merge duplicates in this are a a
2 CONC round Harald "Blue Tooth" I am leaving these two wives as I dont kn ow a
2 CONC bout them, if anyone has info Email me LFHamm@gmail.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes from Pusch file >> ID: I044238 Name: HERBASTUS II (SEE NOTES) D E A
2 CONC RQUE DE CREPON>> Sex: M ALIA: HARALD II (SEE NOTES) GORMSSON OF /DE NMA
2 CONC RK>>/ Title: FORESTER DE ARQUE Name: AKA HERFASTUS FORESTER DE ARQU E>> N
2 CONC ame: AKA HERBASTUS DE CREPON>> Birth: BET 910 AND 1002 in NORMAND Y, FR
2 CONC ANCE Death: BET 1 NOV 981 AND 1002 Event: 1 AKA HAROLD BLAANTAN D KING D
2 CONC E DENMARK>> Event: 2 AKA HERBASTUS OR HERFASTUS DE ARQUE DE CR EPON DE L
2 CONC A ARCHES>> Note:
2 CONT SOME SOURCES SAY HERBASTUS'S FATHER WAS HERFAST DE CREPON OF ARQUE>>.O T
2 CONC HER SOURCES SAY HIS FATHER WAS RANULF GORMSSON DE LA ARCHES>>.
2 CONT
2 CONT Harold Bluetooth (died about 985), king of Denmark (940&#00063;-985) , w
2 CONC ho consolidated the Danish realm as a unitary kingdom. He was the s on o
2 CONC f Gorm the Old (d. about 940) and inherited his kingdom, centere d on J
2 CONC elling in Jutland. Although he temporarily (974-983) lost southe rn Jut
2 CONC land to Holy Roman Emperor Otto II, Harold secured all Denmark u nder h
2 CONC is control and extended his rule to much of Norway. Baptized i n 960 an
2 CONC d thus introducing Christianity into Denmark, he had the famou s Jellin
2 CONC g rune stone erected in his parents' memory. Harold was fatall y wounde
2 CONC d during a rebellion by his son and successor, Sweyn I.
2 CONT
2 CONT King Harald Bluetooth lived in Denmark between 910-940 AD, and was th e s
2 CONC on of Gorm.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contrary to popular opinion, Bluetooth or "Blåtand" as it was in old V i
2 CONC king language had nothing to do with a blue tooth.
2 CONT
2 CONT It means dark complexion - he had very dark hair, which was unusual fo r V
2 CONC ikings. Not only did Harald not fit the classic image physically, h e w
2 CONC as a rather unusual Viking.
2 CONT
2 CONT That is, if your understanding was that the life of a Viking was all b a
2 CONC ttles and pillage. The good King Harald brought Christianity to Scand i
2 CONC navia and also "united" Denmark and Norway. And while we are destroyi n
2 CONC g long-held beliefs, Vikings did not have horns on their helmets!
2 CONT
2 CONT Much of Harald's history was learnt from two runic stones erected to h i
2 CONC s memory in the town of Jelling in Denmark
2 CONT
2 CONT http://worldconnect.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi&#00063;op=GET&db=pusc h
2 CONC &id=I122752
2 CONT
2 CONT 1  NAME Herbastus /de Crepon/ 2  SOUR S033320 3  DATA 4  TEXT Date o f I
2 CONC mport: Jan 17, 2001 1  BIRT 2  DATE ABT. 905 2  PLAC Crepon, Denmar k
2 CONT
2 CONT [De La Pole.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: Antiquities of Shropshire, Vol. 4; Norr; RC 166; Kraentzler 1 1
2 CONC 56, 1194, 1443, 1486.
2 CONT RC: Herbastus de Crepon, Forester of Arques. K: Herbastus "The Dane."
2 CONT Antiquities: Quidam e genere Dansorum. (But I can't read Latin).
2 CONT K: Herbastus de Crepon.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES:
2 CONT 1.  Stuart, Roderick W.  _Royalty for Commoners_.  2nd Edition. Baltim o
2 CONC re,
2 CONT MD: Genealogical Publishing Company, Inc., 1992; line 166-33.  He wa s t
2 CONC he
2 CONT Forester of Arques.
2 CONT
2 CONT Harald refused to accept the crown until he had first performed his fa t
2 CONC her's obsequies with all the magnificence becoming his high rank. On e o
2 CONC f his earliest was the conquest of Norway, which became a provinc e of D
2 CONC enmark. Styrbear, King of Sweden, solicited the aid of King Haro ld in o
2 CONC ne of his wars, and to enforce his request he brought along wit h him G
2 CONC yntha, his sister, a lady of admirable beauty. The stratagem ha d the i
2 CONC ntended effect; Harold Bluetooth became enamored and married he r. The p
2 CONC rogress of Christianity gained some headway during his reign , and the K
2 CONC ing received baptism, and erected a splendid church. His da ughter Guni
2 CONC lda married Richard I, Duke of Normandy.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOME SOURCES SAY HERBASTUS'S FATHER WAS HERFAST DE CREPON OF ARQUE>>.
2 CONT
2 CONT OTHER SOURCES SAY HIS FATHER WAS RANULF GORMSSON DE LA ARCHES>>.
