1 NOTE  These 2 "Gunnora's always confused me due to the name Gunnora being wh e
2 CONC re they were in index. I hope it it right----Email LFHamm@gmail.com w i
2 CONC th info .
2 CONT
2 CONT 1  NAME Gunnora (Gunnor) /de Crepon/ 2  SOUR S033320 3  DATA 4  TEXT D a
2 CONC te of Import: Jan 17, 2001 1  BIRT 2  DATE ABT. 942 2  PLAC of, Norma n
2 CONC dy, France 2  SOUR S033320 3  DATA 4  TEXT Date of Import: Jan 17, 20 0
2 CONC 1 1  DEAT 2  DATE 1031 2  PLAC ,France 2  SOUR S033320 3  DATA 4  TEX T D
2 CONC ate of Import: Jan 17, 2001
2 CONT
2 CONT [De La Pole.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: RC 24, 89, 166, 168, 222; Kraentzler 1153, 1156, 1174, 1180 , 1
2 CONC 194, 1211, 1432, 1443; A. Roots 121E; Coe; Norr; Onslow; Pfafman; D avi
2 CONC s.
2 CONT Roots: (Danish wife) Gunnor, died 1027 or 1031, daughter of forester o f A
2 CONC rques.
2 CONT K. calls her Gonnor de Crepon. Norr: Gunnor (Gunora), (952)-1031.
2 CONT Onslow in "The Dukes of Normandy and Their Orgin" says:
2 CONT Richard I heard about a charming woman married to the superintendent o f f
2 CONC orests at Secheville near Arques. Richard visited Secheville, met t he f
2 CONC orester's beautiful wife, Sainfrida, and "had the impudence to sug gest t
2 CONC o her husband that he should be allowed to make her better acqua intanc
2 CONC e.
2 CONT "The poor man was much perturbed and went in trouble to his wife. Th e l
2 CONC ady had no mind to become the mistress of the Duke, but her moral s wer
2 CONC e not so rigid as to prevent her from making capital our of the s ituat
2 CONC ion for her family. Sainfrida had three sisters, Gunnor, Adelin a and V
2 CONC eva (Wevia), and a brother named Herfast. Gunnor was a very pre tty gir
2 CONC l and by no means particular. Sainfrida told her husband to pre tend to f
2 CONC all in with the Duke's proposals and give Richard facilitie s to pay he
2 CONC r a visit. But when Richard arrived, Gunnor took Sainfrida' s place. Th
2 CONC e Duke did not discover the trick until the following day ; but so deli
2 CONC ghted was he with Gunnor that not only did he forgive Sai nfrida, but t
2 CONC hanked her for having saved him from mortal sin! The resu lt was that G
2 CONC unnor became his wife by Danish custom and eventually th e mother of a n
2 CONC umerous family, the eldest of which was Richard II of N ormandy."
2 CONT Gunnor apparently had children by Richard before they were married an d b
2 CONC efore his marriage to Emma. Evidently the Richard-Gunnor union wa s leg
2 CONC itimized later.
2 CONT RC 166 says Gunnor's father was Herbastus de Crepon, Forester of Arque s (
2 CONC in Denmark). Were there two foresters, the father of Gunnor and Sai nfr
2 CONC ida and also the husband of Sainfrida&#00063; Or did the story beco me t
2 CONC angled over the years&#00063;
2 CONT Coe spells name Gunore.
2 CONT Davis: Gonnor, daughter of a forester of Sauqueville in Britanny. Seco n
2 CONC d wife of Richard I. She married (2) Eperleng, "farmer" of the mill s o
2 CONC f Pitres.
2 CONT
2 CONT *****
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES:
2 CONT 1.  Wingate, John.  _William the Conqueror_, genealogical tables and n o
2 CONC tes.
2 CONT Gunnor was the sister of Herfast of Denmark.  She was the mistress, or
2 CONT wife "by the Danish custom" of Richard I, Duke of Normandy, and marrie d
2 CONT him after the death of his wife, Emma.  She had both legitimate and
2 CONT illegitimate children by Richard.
2 CONT 2.  Douglas, David C.  _William the Conqueror_: The Norman Impact Upon
2 CONT England_.  Berkeley and Los Angeles: University of California Press,
2 CONT 1964; page 145.  He calls Gunnor the sister of Herfast and the aunt o f      O
2 CONC sbern, the steward of William the Conqueror's father, Duke Rob ert.
2 CONT 3.  Stuart, Roderick W.  _Royalty for Commoners_.  2nd Edition. Baltim o
2 CONC re,
2 CONT MD: Genealogical Publishing Company, Inc., 1992; lines 89-1 and 166-33 .
2 CONT 4.  Norr, Vernon M.  _Some Early English Pedigrees_, page 60, generati o
2 CONC n 38,
2 CONT and page 23a.  States that Richard I had issue by and later md (2) (af t
2 CONC er
2 CONT Agnes died) Gunora, b. 952, d. 1031; sister of a forester's wife whom
2 CONT Richard desired but who tricked him with her younger sister.
2 CONT 5.  Ancestral File (AFN:9HMD-WL).  One line gives her birth date as "a b
2 CONC t 935"
2 CONT and only refers to her as "Concubine 1".  She is also shown with the
2 CONT following other parents in the Ancestral File (AFN:FLGR-TL):
2 CONT Herbastus /DE CREPON/ (AFN:FLGR-SF) and Herbastus De C /MRS./
