2 CONT Roots:  William de Warenne, Earl of Warren and 2nd Earl of Surrey.Foug h
2 CONC t in Normandy in 1090 and at Tenchefrai, 1106. Died 1138.  Second hus b
2 CONC and of Isabel.
2 CONT RC: Probably died 11 May 1138.
2 CONT K: William de Warenne II, 2nd Earl of Surrey.
2 CONT Booklet: William de Warenne, 2nd Earl of Surrey, died 1135.
2 CONT
2 CONT This nobleman, William de Warrenne (Earl of Warrenne), 2nd Earl of Sur r
2 CONC ey, joined Robert de Belesmé, Earl of Arundel and Shrewsbury, in favo u
2 CONC r of Robert Curthose against Henry I, and in consequence forfeited hi s E
2 CONC nglish earldom and estates, but those were subsequently restored t o hi
2 CONC m and he was ever afterwards a good and faithful subject to King H enry
2 CONC .  His lordship m. Isabel, dau. of Hugh the Great, Earl of Vermand ois, a
2 CONC nd widow of Robert, Earl of Mellent, by whom he had issue, Willi am, Re
2 CONC ginald, Ralph, Gundred, and Adeline.  The earl d. 11 May, 1138 , and wa
2 CONC s s. by his eldest son, William de Warrenne, 3rd Earl of Surre y. [SirB
2 CONC ernard Burke, Dormant, Abeyant, Forfeited, and Extinct Peerage s, Burke
2 CONC 'sPeerage, Ltd., London, 1883, p. 569, Warren, Earls of Surrey ]
