2 CONT William de Warrenne (Earl of Warrenne), 3rd Earl of Surrey, zealousl y e
2 CONC spoused the cause of King Stephen and had a chief command in the ar my o
2 CONC f that monarch in the battle fought at Lincoln between him and th e adh
2 CONC erents of the Empress Maud.  His lordship m. Adela, dau. of Willi amTal
2 CONC vace, son of Robert de Belesmé, Earl of Shrewsbury, and had by he r (wh
2 CONC o m. 2ndly, Patrick de Evreux, Earl of Salisbury) had an only dau . and h
2 CONC eir, Isabel. In 1147, the Earl of Warrenne and Surrey assumed t he cros
2 CONC s and accompanied Louis, King of France, to the Holy Land again st the S
2 CONC aracens. From this unfortunate enterprise the earl never retur ned, but w
2 CONC hether he fell in battle or died in captivity has not been a scertained
2 CONC . [Sir Bernard Burke, Dormant, Abeyant, Forfeited, and Extin ct Peerage
2 CONC s, Burke's Peerage, Ltd., London, 1883, p. 569, Warren, Earl s of Surre
2 CONC y]
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Norr; Kraentzler 1146, 1333; Norr and K: William de Warren III , T
2 CONC hird Earl of Surrey.
