1 NOTE  Eystein, we are told, was succeeded by his son Halfdan the Generous an d
2 CONC the Stingy of Food.  Halfdan gained this title by paying his mengener o
2 CONC usly in coin but poorly in food.  He died of a malady, was dulyburie d i
2 CONC n a mound beside his father Eystein, and was succeeded by his sonGu dro
2 CONC d.  Gudrod is considered to be a historical personage, although the tal
2 CONC es that are told about him are no doubt at least partly legendary.
2 CONT
