1 CHAN
2 DATE 2 NOV 2019
1 NOTE  Gudrod, "the Magnificent", also called "the Hunting-King", son of Half d
2 CONC an "White-Leg" and Asa (Moriarty) (Sturleson says great grandson of H a
2 CONC lfdan "White-leg"), King of Vermaland, Vestfold and Vingulmark, murde r
2 CONC ed 810-827 at instigation of (2) wife Asa in revenge for forcibly abd u
2 CONC cting her and killing c 800 her father and brother; m. (1) Alfhilde , d
2 CONC aughter of Alfrim, ruler of Vingulmark; m. (2) Asa, daughter of Har ald "
2 CONC Red-Beard", King of Agdir.  Asa is believed buried in the Oseber g ship
2 CONC , the richest Scandinavian archeological find.  [Ancestral Roots ]
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: My line agrees with Sturleson (Gudrod is great grandson of Halfd a
2 CONC n) and not Moriarty (where Gudrod is son of Halfdan).
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------- -
2 CONC ---  ------------------------
2 CONT Following Information copied from Wayne Iverson, World Connect db=wive r
2 CONC srm, rootsweb.com
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------- -
2 CONC ---  ------------------------
2 CONT Also recorded as Godefrid, the sixth king of Haithabu, murdered in 810 .
2 CONT
2 CONT He made war on King Harald Redbeard Herbrandsson and killed Harald an d h
2 CONC is son Gyrd and took a great booty and Harald's daughter, Asa, wh o he m
2 CONC arried.  A year after the birth of son Halfdan, Gudrod was ancho red in S
2 CONC tiflu Sound where a great banquet was given for him and he bec ame very d
2 CONC runk.  Upon going on land at the pier, a man leapt at him an d speared h
2 CONC im through, killing him.  The killer was immediately slai n and in the m
2 CONC orning they found it was Queen Asa's page.  Son Olaf suc ceeded his fat
2 CONC her and later he and Halfdan, Asa's son, divided the kin gdom.
