2 DATE 2 NOV 2019
1 NOTE  EARLDOM of ORKNEY [NOR] - subject to King of Norway until after 1379
2 CONT
2 CONT Jarl Ragnvald then gave the Earldom to his next [illegitimate] son, Ei n
2 CONC ar I (called Turf-Einar because he introduced the use of turf as fue l a
2 CONC mong his islanders), and gave him one longship and manned it for hi s u
2 CONC se. Einar went to Shetland to gather a force, and thence south to t he O
2 CONC rkneys, which had been occupied by the Danish pirates, Thori Tree- bear
2 CONC d and Kalf Skurfa, both of whom he killed circa 894. Halfdan Haale g, K
2 CONC ing Harald Haarfagri5s son, unexpectedly raided Orkney after the b urni
2 CONC ng of Jarl Ragnvald circa 894, and Turf-Einar fled, but returned , surp
2 CONC rised Halfdan, defeated him, and next day captured him and cu t a "spre
2 CONC ad-eagle" or "erne" upon his back in order to avenge Jarl Rag nvald. Ki
2 CONC ng Harald Haarfagri came with a fleet to the Orkneys circa 89 5, and co
2 CONC llected a fine of 60 marks of gold from Jarl Turf-Einar for t he slaugh
2 CONC ter of his son Halfdan Haaleg. The name of Jarl Turf-Einar5 s wife and t
2 CONC he date of his death are not recorded; but he "ruled ove r the Orkneys f
2 CONC or a long time and died of sickness." He had 3 sons: Ar nkel, Erlend I a
2 CONC nd Thorfinn.  [Complete Peerage, X:Appendix A:4-5]
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The following was copied from Martha Jane Hicks web information.  I us e
2 CONC d her pedigree for portions of my own Scandinavian pedigrees:
2 CONT
2 CONT The data in this section of royal Norwegian genealogy was compiled b y h
2 CONC istorians, Anders Stilloff, and Ola Robøle Hegge of Norway and pres ent
2 CONC ed in chart format by Carl M. Ringen Gunderson. The lineage present ed h
2 CONC ere was given to me as part of my ancestry by genealogist Betty Ro cksw
2 CONC old, associated with the Valdres Samband Lag organization. When as ked a
2 CONC bout the research done on the lineage, she said: "It would tak e a 'vol
2 CONC ume' to describe the connections to royalty of the Kvåle line. " She go
2 CONC es on to say that she sent a copy of the material to her skept ic cousi
2 CONC n, Herman Nettum, in East Toten who is a noted genealogist. Af ter exam
2 CONC ination of the chart, which Betty says she is sure he went ove r with a '
2 CONC fine tooth comb' hunting for errors, his only criticism wa s that, whil
2 CONC e the lineage was correct, no one knows the first name o f Earl Thorfin
2 CONC n Sigurdson's wife which was listed as being Ingeborg. I t appears that t
2 CONC he lineage in this database links to Scandinavian roya lty insofar as t
2 CONC he genealogy accounts written by the medieval writer s is correct. The v
2 CONC ice consul of Norway, Lars Løberg, says that the me dieval writers, mos
2 CONC t notably Snorri Sturluson, may have had a politica l motive for presen
2 CONC ting the royal line as an old Norwegian dynasty. Si nce the lineage in t
2 CONC his database ties to the traditionally accepted ro yalty line, it is pr
2 CONC esented here.)
2 CONT
2 CONT [Martha Jane Hicks - mjhicks1, worldconnect.rootsweb.com]
