1 NAME Thorfinn"Skull Cleaver" /Orkney/
2 GIVN Thorfinn"Skull Cleaver"
2 SURN Orkney
1 SEX M
1 _UID 5F9E461467EE447CB70E958EB72A9D9668A4
1 _AMTID 162143285915:1030:164657654
1 CHAN
2 DATE 2 NOV 2019
1 NOTE  EARLDOM of ORKNEY [NOR] - subject to King of Norway until after 1379
2 CONT
2 CONT Arnkel, Erlend I and Thorfinn I on the death of their father Jarl Turf -
2 CONC Einar succeeded as co-Jarls of Orkney. Arnkel and Erlend were old eno u
2 CONC gh to be taken into western piracy by King Eric Bloodaxe 939, and Tho r
2 CONC finn5s son Arnfinn was of an age to marry a woman of perhaps twenty-s e
2 CONC ven in 954 or 955.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thorfinn I Hausakliffer (Skull-cleaver) became sole Jarl of Orkney i n 9
2 CONC 54 and again 955 until 976, when Gunnhild and her surviving sons Ra gnf
2 CONC red and Gudred came to Orkney with their adherents after the defea t an
2 CONC d death of King Harald II Greyfell at Limfiord. They departed agai n in 9
2 CONC 77 and Jarl Thorfinn seems to have died soon, afterwards. He m. , 941, G
2 CONC relod, dau. of Dungad or Duncan, Mormaer of Caithness, by Groa , dau. o
2 CONC f Thorstein the Red (e), and had issue, Arnfinn, Havard, Hlodv e, Lint a
2 CONC nd Skuli. Although Heimskringla in one place suggests that th e brother
2 CONC s were "Jarls there" simultaneously, the Orkneyinga Saga, an d Heimskri
2 CONC ngla in another place make it clear that four of them rule d in success
2 CONC ion each as sole Jarl.  [Complete Peerage, X:Appendix A:6]
2 CONT
2 CONT (e) Thorstein the Red m. Thorida, daughter of Eyvind Austmann, the Eas t
2 CONC erling, by Rafertach, daughter of Cearbhall MacDunghal, King of Ossor y 8
2 CONC 42 to 888 and King of Dublin 873 to 888.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: By the statement concerning Arnfinn's marrying a 27 year old i n 9
2 CONC 54/955, CP seems to put serious doubt as to the marriage date of "9 41" f
2 CONC or Thorfinn & Grelod.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: I assume that Arnkel & Erlend were the 7th & 8th Jarl of Orkney , r
2 CONC espectively.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Curt Hofemann, curt_hofemann@yahoo.com, added the following speculatio n
2 CONC s concerning the marriage/birth dates:
2 CONT
2 CONT Pure speculation on my part, but maybe there was a politically arrange d m
2 CONC arriage agreement made when Arnfinn was very young & that he wasn5 t of m
2 CONC arriageable age (13) until 954/5.  955 - 13 = DOB of 942 which w ould f
2 CONC it perfectly for his parents to have married in 941.  Note als o that 9
2 CONC 54 was when Ragnhild5s father, Eric Bloodaxe, was killed wit h Arnfinn5
2 CONC s 2 uncles & Eric5s wife & family fled back to Orkney.  Perh aps it was a w
2 CONC in-win for both families.  Ranghild (now without land/ti tle) married t
2 CONC he future Jarl of Orkney & Caithness & Arnfinn married t he dau of the f
2 CONC ormer king of Norway, former king of Northumberland & g rand dau of the k
2 CONC ings of Denmark & Norway.  Then again, Ragnhild had A rnfinn murdered, s
2 CONC o I guess she didn5t think it was such a win-win  ;> (
2 CONT
2 CONT Regards,
2 CONT Curt
