1 NOTE  EARLDOM of ORKNEY [NOR] - subject to King of Norway until after 1379
2 CONT
2 CONT Hlodve, who had previously m. Audna, Edna or Ethne, da. of "Kiarval, t h
2 CONC e Irish King," (f) who seems to have protected him from his sister-in -
2 CONC law, and had issue a son, Sigurd Digri, and two daughters. He d. in h i
2 CONC s bed circa 988, and was bur, at Hofn in Caithness. He was succeede d b
2 CONC y his only recorded son,  [Complete Peerage, X:Appendix A:7-8]
2 CONT
2 CONT (f) Kiarval has not been identified.  J. Anderson suggests Cearbhall , K
2 CONC ing of Dublin and Ossory, but that prince d. 888.
