1 NOTE  Malcolm took advantage of the fact that the English were preoccupied w i
2 CONC th Danish raids and marched south, winning the Battle of Carham again s
2 CONC t the Angles in 1018 and thereby regaining Lothian.  Thirteen years l a
2 CONC ter King Canute invaded Scotland and forced Malcolm to submit to him .  H
2 CONC owever, Canute seems to have recognized Malcolm's possession of Lo thia
2 CONC n.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Malcolm II's reign, Scottish succession was based on the princip l
2 CONC e of direct descent.  Previously, succession was determined by tanist r
2 CONC y - during a king's lifetime an heir was chosen and known as "tanaist e r
2 CONC ig" (second to the king).
