1 NOTE  [Carelton-Stickney.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Ralph Neville, K.G. who was created First Earl of Westmoreland,
2 CONT September 20, 1397 and who 1st married Margaret, 9 June 1396,
2 CONT daughter of Sir Hugh Stafford , K.G. 2nd earl of Stafford.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Ralph Neville 2nd married Joan de Beaufort, daughter of John of
2 CONT Gaunt - duke of Lancaster and granddaughter of King Edward III of
2 CONT England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Perhaps the Westmoreland in Shakespeare's 'Henry V.'  He was the 1st E a
2 CONC rl Westmoreland.
2 CONT
2 CONT born c. 1364
2 CONT died Oct. 21, 1425, Raby Castle, Durham, Eng.
2 CONT
2 CONT Neville also spelled Nevill
2 CONT English noble who, though created earl by King Richard II , supporte d t
2 CONC he usurpation of the crown by Henry IV and di d much to establish t he L
2 CONC ancastrian dynasty.
2 CONT The eldest son of John, 3rd Baron Neville, he was knighte d during a F r
2 CONC ench expedition in 1380, succeeded to his fath er's barony in 1388, a n
2 CONC d was created Earl of Westmorland o n Sept. 29, 1397. Further royal f a
2 CONC vours failed to command h is allegiance, and in 1399 he joined his br o
2 CONC ther-in-law, He nry of Lancaster (later Henry IV), in securing the de p
2 CONC ositi on of Richard II. As the new king's kinsman (by his secon d mar r
2 CONC iage, to Joan Beaufort, half sister to Henry) and a s a useful counte r
2 CONC balance to the strength of the Percy fami ly in the North, Neville co u
2 CONC ld expect suitable rewards. I n September 1399 he was made marshal o f E
2 CONC ngland and in Octo ber was granted for life the valuable honour o f Ric
2 CONC hmond, Y orkshire. In 1403 he helped suppress the Percy rebellio n i n t
2 CONC he North, and in 1405 he intercepted rebel forces at Shipton Mo or, nea
2 CONC r York, and tricked them into surrender: th e rising in Yorkshi re thus l
2 CONC ost much strength.
2 CONT Neville had now become very experienced in Scottish affairs , having l o
2 CONC ng been a warden of the West March of Scotland , and was charged wit h t
2 CONC he safekeeping of the northern bord er during Henry V's absences i n Fr
2 CONC ance. Hence, he took no p art in the Battle of Agincourt in 1415 ( thou
2 CONC gh Shakespear e thought he was present) or in later French campaig ns b
2 CONC u t was a member of the Council of Regency under John, Duke o f Be dfor
2 CONC d, in 1415.
2 CONT Copyright `1994-2002 Encyclopædia Britannica, Inc.
2 CONT His Family Was One The Most Powerful In England And Shar ed Dominatio n T
2 CONC he Northern Counties With The Percy Family
2 CONT His Daughter Cecily Neville Married Richard, Duke York , And Became Th e M
2 CONC other Edward IV And Richard III
2 CONT His Second Wife Was Joan Beaufort, Daughter John Gaun t And Half Siste r H
2 CONC enry Lancaster (Later Henry Iv).
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the 1st Earl of Westmorland, and the Knight of The Garter.
2 CONT
